{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game","id":1203337,"title":"Disconnect between sorcery in lore and the encouraged use in game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-05T02:30:07-07:00","id":1203337,"title":"Disconnect between sorcery in lore and the encouraged use in game","content":"In the lore sorcery is always presented as a dramatic, life altering procedure, in 2e especially but certainly still in 3e. On the other hand in my experience a combination of the lack of good spells beyond the one attack spell you need and the variance of attributes needed for spell casting and the complete lack of charms strongly discourages specialized sorcerers instead causing people to usually just dip it for a single spell or two which doesn't seem to fit he lore at all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T02:57:46-07:00","id":1203345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game#post1203337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the lack of good spells beyond the one attack spell you need</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's a matter of opinion.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the complete lack of charms</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd I'm not sure what this refers to.<br /> <br /> \u200bRegardless: the way that sorcery works now, with the shaping rituals and associated unique Supernatural Merits, the possible transformative effects of your control spell(s), and the more freeform capacity to create sorcerous workings, sorcery is certainly a more profound alteration even if you aren't heavily invested in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T03:09:36-07:00","id":1203349,"title":"","content":"For my most recent PC, his initiation into sorcery was <i>literally</i> transformative, as when the god who owned the library discovered that my character had been sneaking in there and reading his sorcerous secrets, the god transfigured the boy into his namesake.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, my character's name was Spider.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">He got better.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T05:53:06-07:00","id":1203376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game#post1203337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the lore sorcery is always presented as a dramatic, life altering procedure, in 2e especially but certainly still in 3e. On the other hand in my experience a combination of the lack of good spells beyond the one attack spell you need and the variance of attributes needed for spell casting and the complete lack of charms strongly discourages specialized sorcerers instead causing people to usually just dip it for a single spell or two which doesn't seem to fit he lore at all</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth to note that PCs are rarely &quot;normal&quot; people in the first place, driven especially, which lends more naturally to sorcery more than most.<br /> <br /> And yeah, we'll disagree on the lack of good spells. You also forget Workings when figuring out the miracles they can bring forth.<br /> The various initiations have a collection to set you apart from other people, so you have both a lore and a mechanical incentive to be &quot;weird&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dunno what you say about complete lack of charms tho. Occult has several charms useful for sorcery, from roll enhancers to expanding ways to figure out sorcery is happening to draining spirits to fuel spells. Given that sorcery is its own thing, that's plenty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T06:24:47-07:00","id":1203389,"title":"","content":"It's understandable that the lack of official content is limiting your options to explore sorcery as a defining character trait. I agree with that. But the system is not limiting by itself, and it definitely encourages deep and powerful sorcerous concepts. As more books are released and more content is created, this problem will solve itself. And then there's always homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T06:30:38-07:00","id":1203392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203389#post1203389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's understandable that the lack of official content is limiting your options to explore sorcery as a defining character trait. I agree with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's a lot more than was ever given in a previous core book.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T06:49:53-07:00","id":1203399,"title":"","content":"I would also say you may be approaching sorcery though the lens of other systems. Sorcery is expressed not just through spells, but through the working systems and the sorcerous initiation rituals. These add a host of uniqueness to the sorcerer. <br /> <br /> Additionally, sorcery spells are designed to encourage different play styles and fit different character thematics. Being a sorcerer is something you are, not something you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T09:17:57-07:00","id":1203429,"title":"","content":"So, my friend is playing a sorceress.<br /> She rules a kingdom of fanatically loyal, 6 1/2 foot people many of whom have some fire magick. They have multiple dragons, hundreds of gryffons and golems. Their mountain kingdom is magically fertile so produces tons of food.<br /> She also has fiery wings she can summon at will, strange viscous fire-blood, jet-black skin with burning white veins, and a heart of fire.<br /> <br /> Oh, also her kingdom has a giant demon-built canal through it.<br /> <br /> All of this she did with sorcery. It seems pretty dramatic and life-altering to me.<br /> <br /> Another friend of mine plays a sorcerer who lives in a giant flying castle with its own sun (which, again, he made with sorcery).<br /> <br /> Now, sure, there are far less spells than charms in the book. But you can do tons with workings. And as Isator said, there's more spells than in the Core for 3rd ed than for 2nd. Yes, we could do with more spells... but hey, a Solar sorcerer at least has some spells. Lunars and Sidereals don't even have any charms!<br /> <br /> Admittedly, a couple of others got like one spell when they were high-XP, but it's not really surprising that when you start going into a new area when you've already got 300xp, it's not a big part of your character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-05-2018, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:02:41-07:00","id":1203570,"title":"","content":"Sorcerous workings are nice but in the absence of any way to bump up your success rate or ways to get more non-charm dice it ends up losing alot of your niche to the far easier to accomplish crafting (Seriously, whoever made the occult charm tree seems to have forgotten how supernals work, namely, you get one)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:09:33-07:00","id":1203574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203429#post1203429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, a couple of others got like one spell when they were high-XP, but it's not really surprising that when you start going into a new area when you've already got 300xp, it's not a big part of your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it should be, shaping rituals are built to take up a lot of &quot;character space&quot; (I'll go through them to illustrate)<br /> Bargan With Mara: You made a deal with the devil (except this one's clingier)<br /> Pact with an Ifrit lord: You passed some grand test from an elemental lord of fire<br /> Scarred by Nightmares: You are forever haunted by nightmares with some mysterious connection to the wyld<br /> Soul-Perfecting Elixir: Soul-Perfecting<br /> The Talisman of Ten-Thousand Eyes: Okay, this could be minor I'll give you that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:14:36-07:00","id":1203578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203570#post1203570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerous workings are nice but in the absence of any way to bump up your success rate or ways to get more non-charm dice it ends up losing alot of your niche to the far easier to accomplish crafting (Seriously, whoever made the occult charm tree seems to have forgotten how supernals work, namely, you get one)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've actually seen much greater success in workings then in crafting. Full excellencies and that one Lore math charm are handy for them, and you don't need magic materials to pull them off. Also, I can't craft the temple I'm in to be possessed by intelleigence and communicate the divine mysteries of my faith to lay people. Or living things in general. Or cursing my enemies/the land. (I've actually had th oppisite: Craft seems way harder, and I've had to clearly define what <i>cant</i> be Workings to make craft viable).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:16:19-07:00","id":1203581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game#post1203337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the lore sorcery is always presented as a dramatic, life altering procedure, in 2e especially but certainly still in 3e. On the other hand in my experience a combination of the lack of good spells beyond the one attack spell you need and the variance of attributes needed for spell casting and the complete lack of charms strongly discourages specialized sorcerers instead causing people to usually just dip it for a single spell or two which doesn't seem to fit he lore at all</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrestrial spells all seem fine to me, albiet not helpful for 'theme' sorcerers at the moment (I can't have a scholar of flame with all fire spells). I've not seen much use of Celestial, can't speak to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:25:05-07:00","id":1203585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203578#post1203578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've actually seen much greater success in workings then in crafting. Full excellencies and that one Lore math charm are handy for them, and you don't need magic materials to pull them off. Also, I can't craft the temple I'm in to be possessed by intelleigence and communicate the divine mysteries of my faith to lay people. Or living things in general. Or cursing my enemies/the land. (I've actually had th oppisite: Craft seems way harder, and I've had to clearly define what <i>cant</i> be Workings to make craft viable).</div> </div> </div> </div>They work fine early game but once you get to celestial 2 or beyond the high goal numbers, lack of any supplementary charms and existence of a terminus causes it to fall behind and quite honestly, I have no idea how you're supposed to accomplish anything inside the solar circle. Additionally, it's just kinda unsatisfying to not have any charms for a ability that's so central to your character, like if the entire craft charm tree didn't actually help with crafting but instead just enhanced your ability to talk with/fight buildings or something (Not my best metaphor I'll admit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:25:31-07:00","id":1203586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203570#post1203570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerous workings are nice but in the absence of any way to bump up your success rate or ways to get more non-charm dice it ends up losing alot of your niche to the far easier to accomplish crafting (Seriously, whoever made the occult charm tree seems to have forgotten how supernals work, namely, you get one)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so our circle crafter actually ran the math, unless you a fully devoted to craft there is a very slim chance of even having a chance of getting legendary projects off the ground. However as a solar performing a solar ambition 3 working I can reasonably get 9, 20 dice (exploding essence 10s) rolls to hit my successes required for the working. That\u2019s not even getting the math lore charm. <br /> <br /> The occult supernal is not about sorcery per se. Solar occult is about illuminating the obscure, reveal that which is hidden, and taming the world of spirits to your will imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:26:45-07:00","id":1203587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203570#post1203570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerous workings are nice but in the absence of any way to bump up your success rate or ways to get more non-charm dice it ends up losing alot of your niche to the far easier to accomplish crafting (Seriously, whoever made the occult charm tree seems to have forgotten how supernals work, namely, you get one)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, the Craft Rewrite Homebrewers say just the opposite: why bother picking up 5 Charms to design and build a Dam when you can just do a working to regulate the Rivers for 50 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:27:26-07:00","id":1203589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203570#post1203570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerous workings are nice but in the absence of any way to bump up your success rate or ways to get more non-charm dice it ends up losing alot of your niche to the far easier to accomplish crafting</div> </div> </div> </div>This requires elaboration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Seriously, whoever made the occult charm tree seems to have forgotten how supernals work, namely, you get one)</div> </div> </div> </div>You get one what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:37:45-07:00","id":1203591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203587#post1203587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ironically, the Craft Rewrite Homebrewers say just the opposite: why bother picking up 5 Charms to design and build a Dam when you can just do a working to regulate the Rivers for 50 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they're right, sorcery up to about celestial one is far too easy because it's balanced around characters with absolutely no charms to enhance their workings, beyond that is becomes rather impossible without collecting an ass-ton of means and such which is obviously more time consuming then using your craft charms to acomplish it with your insane number of awesome charms to enhance crafting. The problem is while crafting requires a massive amount of character investment sorcery doesn't really allow for any<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T17:41:48-07:00","id":1203592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203589#post1203589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get one what?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry that was vague, the problem is the entire (And I do mean entire) occult charm tree is dedicated to doing something to spirits which, while pretty nice when fighting spirits (though still not as nice as it should be for the investment imo) leaves you at a severe disadvantage when dealing with anything else, which is understandable, excluding sorcery spirits are just about the only thing you have though I'd probably design it more toward using spirits to accomplish x as opposed to just fucking with spirits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T18:39:00-07:00","id":1203609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203591#post1203591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And they're right, sorcery up to about celestial one is far too easy because it's balanced around characters with absolutely no charms to enhance their workings, beyond that is becomes rather impossible without collecting an ass-ton of means and such which is obviously more time consuming then using your craft charms to acomplish it with your insane number of awesome charms to enhance crafting. The problem is while crafting requires a massive amount of character investment sorcery doesn't really allow for any<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that Solar workings can more readily accomplish a number of things that crafting even Artifacts cannot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T18:42:37-07:00","id":1203613,"title":"","content":"Wow, I think this is the first time i\u2019ve seen anyone suggest that Sorcery wasn\u2019t a good enough option for 3E PCs. I feel like i\u2019ve fallen down some kind of rabbit hole. Usually the critique is that it\u2019s too good and thus is incentivized for characters it doesn\u2019t fit!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T18:45:19-07:00","id":1203614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203613#post1203613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I think this is the first time i\u2019ve seen anyone suggest that Sorcery wasn\u2019t a good enough option for 3E PCs. I feel like i\u2019ve fallen down some kind of rabbit hole. Usually the critique is that it\u2019s too good and thus is incentivized for characters it doesn\u2019t fit!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's too good for a single charm but too weak to be anything you want to make key to your character,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T18:46:01-07:00","id":1203615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203609#post1203609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI think that Solar workings can more readily accomplish a number of things that crafting even Artifacts cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that requires actually performing that working","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T18:55:25-07:00","id":1203620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203615#post1203615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that requires actually performing that working</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeeees?<br /> <br /> \u200bIf there are examples in which Craft does not in fact provide an alternative, and you want to do the thing, than doubling down and working on it is your only recourse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:05:52-07:00","id":1203624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203620#post1203620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeeeees?<br /> <br /> \u200bIf there are examples in which Craft does not in fact provide an alternative, and you want to do the thing, than doubling down and working on it is your only recourse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Performing a solar circle working is hard, incredibly so and because there is no way to increase your abilities you're stuck with putting an immense amount of work into collecting dozens of means in order to get your 10-5 successes to complete the working before your terminus, my point is there is no way to balance sorcery as it is now, either it's as powerful as the one charm investiture would allow at which point is must be a footnote on your character or it's powerful enough to be the basis of your character (As the lore implies) at which point it's ludicriously op because one charm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:13:37-07:00","id":1203626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203585#post1203585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They work fine early game but once you get to celestial 2 or beyond the high goal numbers, lack of any supplementary charms and existence of a terminus causes it to fall behind and quite honestly, I have no idea how you're supposed to accomplish anything inside the solar circle. Additionally, it's just kinda unsatisfying to not have any charms for a ability that's so central to your character, like if the entire craft charm tree didn't actually help with crafting but instead just enhanced your ability to talk with/fight buildings or something (Not my best metaphor I'll admit)</div> </div> </div> </div>So, crunching numbers on success of sorcerery: <br /> A Solar at E5 is going to (for my purposes) have maxed out his Int and Occult, and probably is operating in his specialty. That's 21 dice per roll(Free excellency charm, if not straight up excellency)<br /> On Terminus 5, you're averaging 9.5 sucesses a roll. You can reach 45~ without charms or additional time. Now, that's enough to Finnesse 1 a Solar working.<br /> <br /> Occult Charms that Help you sorcery:<br /> <br /> Ancient Tounge understanding gives you some successes, which would replace your excellency 2-1. I...don't know what that does to your odds, except guarenteeing a no botch of Finesse 1 and 3.<br /> <br /> There's the free excellncy, not really worth commenting on.<br /> <br /> Six Eternities Travail gives exploding tens, for Essence 10s. I...again, don't know how much that helps. Hm. Off the top of my head, that means every die has a 1/10 chance of giving you another die, so you average to 2 bonus die on each roll, bringing your total rolled die to 23, and 10.5 successes? Math people, help.<br /> <br /> The Lore charm gives 5 bonus die here, bringing us to 26-28 die, adding 2 expected successes per roll, for a total of 55~ successes w/o means.<br /> <br /> Means:<br /> <br /> You 100% can get 2 of these every working IMHO (Abillitis and Spells), if your clever. Exotic components is another likely one.Extra time is a pain in a half in my experience, but we'll add it to. that's 4.. So, we are working with 9 rolls of around 11 sucesses on avergae. 99 sucesses, meaning a Solar working is well within reach. <br /> <br /> NOW, I'm not 100% sure on the math (I don't do this often) but I think that this makes solar workings easy for Solar sorcerers. The effect of the Lore charm is decrease w/essence of course.<br /> <br /> I recall a long, long time ago having a drawn out fight over whether &quot;a sorcerer&quot; was a coherent concept and therefore worth having a supernal to focus on the way craft is. I stand by my statement then that it's not in it of itself. A sorcerer needs more defintion to have meaningful investements, as reflected by getting a means for abillities. Occult is sorcerery light to encourage sorcerers to branch or be other traits. I do think, via shaping rituals and merits, sorcery can quickly be character defining. It has been for all the sorcerers I've seen, but maybe I'm just lucky in that regard (the sorcerers were: A fire priest, Queen of Ysyr, a jungle shaman, an artifact dealer, a wandering monk pursuing enlightment, and a scholar of the fae given a comission by Saturn).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:17:02-07:00","id":1203628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203614#post1203614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's too good for a single charm but too weak to be anything you want to make key to your character,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Workings requiring... well... work... make them more central to characters exploring sorcery, not less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:18:41-07:00","id":1203630,"title":"","content":"You are aware spirits those spirits and occult charms can be directed towards additional means right? I mean you want to do a working to regulate a river's flooding and yet somehow avoid the normal problems that creating a damn causes. River god, field god, maybe the local city god could be leveraged to assist in that, and having charms that can enable you to find them, speak to them, and if needed threaten them might help in reaching that point. You want to create a ward around a place to help defend against spirits? I would certainly say the ability to use Unnatural Perception Technique or Keen Unnatural Eye can be used as a means to make the ward more effective for alerting people to the presence of those spirits. Spirit-Repelling Diagram would be an obvious aid in that manner.<br /> <br /> This is assuming your ST doesn't give you the bonus for Ancient Tongue Understanding on workings when it works on shaping rituals. Though I've seen nothing that implies one can't add their excellency to those checks normally.<br /> <br /> Just saying Occult not being confined entirely to sorcerery does not make either less.<br /> <br /> Addendum: I'm sorry are you arguing that Solar Workings aren't good because they aren't easy to pull off, Hamster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:21:43-07:00","id":1203632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203624#post1203624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Performing a solar circle working is hard, incredibly so and because there is no way to increase your abilities you're stuck with putting an immense amount of work into collecting dozens of means in order to get your 10-5 successes to complete the working before your terminus</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, as I recall, one is sharply limited in how many Means can actually be incorporated into a working.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd say that Solar workings have a tendency to have lower Finesse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">my point is there is no way to balance sorcery as it is now, either it's as powerful as the one charm investiture would allow at which point is must be a footnote on your character or it's powerful enough to be the basis of your character (As the lore implies) at which point it's ludicriously op because one charm</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is a silly point. The balance of sorcery comes in the need to actually buy those spells one at a time (for a not insignificant amount of XP), and how the more freeform workings system comes with its own costs and difficulties. Maybe some of the capabilities one might acquire from their original initiation are a bit unusual as something that would extend from a single Charm purchase, but I'd say that's an area that can be fudged.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, judging the utility of sorcery based on the mechanical conceit of initiation taking the form of a Charm purchase is ludicrous. Honestly, Terrestrial Circle Sorcery is barely an actual Exalted Charm; it's mostly just a mechanical representation of one's path of initiation into the wider world of sorcery.<br /> <br /> You appear to know enough about sorcery to make reasonably detailed comments on how workings function, and yet seem to be neglecting to actually look at what it can do in making your assessment of it.<br /> <br /> \u200bSorcery, as it has been provided in the Third Edition core book, is perfectly capable of being a fully realised central aspect of a character <b>and</b>, even if a player makes minimal investment into it, conveys enough capability and weird quality at the most basic level to let a character be recognizably a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn contrast with prior Editions, in which somebody actually could just buy Death of Obsidian Butterflies and Emerald Countermagic, hardly ever use them, and thus be nigh indistinguishable from any non-sorcerous character.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:34:43-07:00","id":1203635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203630#post1203630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are aware spirits those spirits and occult charms can be directed towards additional means right? I mean you want to do a working to regulate a river's flooding and yet somehow avoid the normal problems that creating a damn causes. River god, field god, maybe the local city god could be leveraged to assist in that, and having charms that can enable you to find them, speak to them, and if needed threaten them might help in reaching that point. You want to create a ward around a place to help defend against spirits? I would certainly say the ability to use Unnatural Perception Technique or Keen Unnatural Eye can be used as a means to make the ward more effective for alerting people to the presence of those spirits. Spirit-Repelling Diagram would be an obvious aid in that manner.<br /> <br /> This is assuming your ST doesn't give you the bonus for Ancient Tongue Understanding on workings when it works on shaping rituals. Though I've seen nothing that implies one can't add their excellency to those checks normally.<br /> <br /> Just saying Occult not being confined entirely to sorcerery does not make either less.<br /> <br /> Addendum: I'm sorry are you arguing that Solar Workings aren't good because they aren't easy to pull off, Hamster?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not whether or not they're easy or hard to accomplish it's their difficulty compared to the alternative, for example, while a terrestial working to monitor rivers is FAR easier than any other solution (provided you have the 2 weeks or so you need) while changing the weather and terrain in a region requires you to be at essence 5 with sorcery (or go do a higher circle but at that point there's little chance of you succeeding or you can make a 1st age terraformer or some such at essense 1/2 with crafting and you just need some jade<br /> <br /> By essence 5 a crafter has dozens of charms dedicated to crafting<br /> By essence 5 a swordsman has tens of charms dedicated to stabby<br /> By essence 5 a bureaucrat has dozens of charms dedicated to bureaucracy<br /> By essence 5 a sorcerer has 3 charms dedicated to sorcery<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23635,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","user":"Lion Hamster","date":". 04-05-2018, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:42:40-07:00","id":1203640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203635#post1203635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not whether or not they're easy or hard to accomplish it's their difficulty compared to the alternative, for example, while a terrestial working to monitor rivers is FAR easier than any other solution (provided you have the 2 weeks or so you need) while changing the weather and terrain in a region requires you to be at essence 5 with sorcery (or go do a higher circle but at that point there's little chance of you succeeding or you can make a 1st age terraformer or some such at essense 1/2 with crafting and you just need some jade</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First Age Artifice requires sorcery however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:44:37-07:00","id":1203641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203640#post1203640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Age Artifice requires sorcery however.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you can have sorcery but not be a sorcerer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:50:19-07:00","id":1203642,"title":"","content":"The core problem (as I've been repeating time and time again across three editions to no avail) is that Sorcery in Exalted offers no real sense of progression beyond the three initiations, which are extremely non-granular, take forever to reach in-game, and are partially or completely unavailable to many splats.<br /> <br /> A master of Melee or Stealth or Lore gets better and better charms the more they invest, expanding their options by progressing through the tree. This encourages investment and makes dedicated masters of those arts reasonable builds.<br /> <br /> Sorcerers get nothing. Giving people a free spell with their initiations, while it seemed like an obvious step, actually makes things <i>worse</i> because now there's simply no down payment to becoming a sorcerer at all - anyone and everyone is encouraged to buy one or two spells, but there's no point (as with high-in-the-tree Melee or MA charms) where you can say &quot;alright, here we can put some really good stuff to reward people who have dedicated themselves intensely to Sorcery.&quot; The most powerful spells you can possibly make can effectively have, at most, a max of <i>two</i> prerequisites, and those two can functionally be any two spells you want. Worse, Sorcery is front-loaded by the control spell system - your first spell is worth the most; others offer less, rewarding dabblers over dedicated Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> The core book didn't even give us a single evocation tree to progress along, it just vaguely implied it exists. If your Sorcerer knows a thousand spells, there is still absolutely no incentive for you to pick up your thousand-and-first spell rather than buying a Melee charm to balance things out (and in practice, since you grab the best spells first, it's less &quot;a thousand spells&quot; and more &quot;two or three spells.&quot;)<br /> <br /> I understand the desire to have different things work mechanically differently, but having every spell be its own disconnected thing with no prerequisites is <i>dumb</i>. It doesn't reflect how Sorcery is portrayed in fiction, where study and progression and research and accumulated knowledge are absolutely central. It doesn't provide any support for playing a <i>sorcerer</i> as an archetype rather than someone who just picked up the few most relevant spells.<br /> <br /> I'm unsure how it can be fixed at this point - it's really something that should have been fixed in the basic design for Sorcery. I guess you can put all the weight on evocations that boost Sorcery, but making and balancing generic Sorcery boosts is extremely difficult and you still don't really have any sense of knowledge-based progression when playing a Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> What I would probably do is just allow spells to have any sort of prerequisites you want (charms, evocations, and other spells), and write off the corebook spells as introductory stuff. That would be a bit crude, but I feel it really is necessary. Without prerequisites there's not really any sense of progressing as a Sorcerer or personalizing them in any particularly deep way - the initiations and control spells just don't cut it compared to the in-depth progression offered by trees in every other part of the game.<br /> <br /> Evocations for sorcery-boosting artifacts <i>might</i> cut it, but again... having some way to progress and benefit from extended mastery of Sorcery in the same way that a warrior can progress and benefit from extended mastery of Melee is a central part of playing a Sorcerer, so it's baffling that it was left out of the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-05-2018, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:52:06-07:00","id":1203644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203632#post1203632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, as I recall, one is sharply limited in how many Means can actually be incorporated into a working.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd say that Solar workings have a tendency to have lower Finesse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bThis is a silly point. The balance of sorcery comes in the need to actually buy those spells one at a time (for a not insignificant amount of XP), and how the more freeform workings system comes with its own costs and difficulties. Maybe some of the capabilities one might acquire from their original initiation are a bit unusual as something that would extend from a single Charm purchase, but I'd say that's an area that can be fudged.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, judging the utility of sorcery based on the mechanical conceit of initiation taking the form of a Charm purchase is ludicrous. Honestly, Terrestrial Circle Sorcery is barely an actual Exalted Charm; it's mostly just a mechanical representation of one's path of initiation into the wider world of sorcery.<br /> <br /> You appear to know enough about sorcery to make reasonably detailed comments on how workings function, and yet seem to be neglecting to actually look at what it can do in making your assessment of it.<br /> <br /> \u200bSorcery, as it has been provided in the Third Edition core book, is perfectly capable of being a fully realised central aspect of a character <b>and</b>, even if a player makes minimal investment into it, conveys enough capability and weird quality at the most basic level to let a character be recognizably a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn contrast with prior Editions, in which somebody actually could just buy Death of Obsidian Butterflies and Emerald Countermagic, hardly ever use them, and thus be nigh indistinguishable from any non-sorcerous character.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with balancing sorcery around needing to buy multiple spells is A: You kinda don't weak workings can do any one offs you need (Corrupted words is never going to be used enough to be worth it) and B: By making spellcasting vary from attribute to attribute your make having a large spell list require investments in wits, perception, intellegence, occult and presence (And also brawl/melee for the armour and claw spells) with no charms to compensate for having the lower attribute/skill penalties that encourages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T19:55:28-07:00","id":1203646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203641#post1203641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you can have sorcery but not be a sorcerer</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How so? A crafter who is iniated into the sacred rites of his god so he can make his flesh bronze and manipulat the cosmos through his smithing is as much a sorcerer as any.<br /> <br /> I guess a good summary of my understanding is I agree with Aquillon(Sorcery lacks a coherent image in exalted, and thus 'a sorcerer' as an archtype beyond 'master of weird' is meaningless), except that that's why I like sorcery and prefer it in this system over casting in Dnd or CoC or Conan's d20 or a handful of others (Exalted's sorcery is contending with Ars for my favorite system). Especially since it can include things like shaman vision quests as much as sorcerers who study under the gaze of Set in Stygia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_b