ch as sorcerers who study under the gaze of Set in Stygia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, a crafter initiated blah blah blah is a crafter, he knows sorcery sure but he's a crafter<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:07:09-07:00","id":1203653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203652#post1203652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree, a crafter initiated blah blah blah is a crafter, he knows sorcery sure but he's a crafter</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough, we'll have to agree to disagree. I think 'sorcerer' and 'crafter' are far from mutually exclusive terms in fiction and folklore, and in fact over lap a great deal. The fact that the pinacle of ancient craft, First Age, required both seems to back that up. What would a sorcerer be then? Is it seperate from an occultist in your defintion?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:08:21-07:00","id":1203654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203647#post1203647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bYou seem to be very confident in making broad statements based on, what, anecdotal evidence? What you reckon? On what basis do you assert that Corrupted Words is never going to be used?</div> </div> </div> </div>The ability to replicate it with a working, while you could permanently spend 10xp to learn corrupted words, you can use a terrestrial circle working to &quot;Take the breath from his lungs and draw away his treacherous words&quot; while there may well be a circumstance where it's worth it 10xp is a hell of a lot for something that <i>might</i> come in handy eventually<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:15:09-07:00","id":1203657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203653#post1203653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough, we'll have to agree to disagree. I think 'sorcerer' and 'crafter' are far from mutually exclusive terms in fiction and folklore, and in fact over lap a great deal. The fact that the pinacle of ancient craft, First Age, required both seems to back that up. What would a sorcerer be then? Is it seperate from an occultist in your defintion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets say for example I make a presence supernal (I did this a few days ago) it might we worth taking a few dots of craft (Painting) to make a few paintings for some subtle social attacks<br /> <br /> On the other hand lets say I make a craft supernal, investing in enough skills to get 5 in multiple forms of craft and harnessing the incredible power of the unconquered sun to allow me to erect cities within days<br /> <br /> Is person one just as much of a crafter as person two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:22:59-07:00","id":1203660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203654#post1203654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The ability to replicate it with a working, while you could permanently spend 10xp to learn corrupted words, you can use a terrestrial circle working to &quot;Take the breath from his lungs and draw away his treacherous words&quot; while there may well be a circumstance where it's worth it 10xp is a hell of a lot for something that <i>might</i> come in handy eventually</div> </div> </div> </div>A working costs exp, requires unique ingredients/rituals and takes a week or more to enact during which time you can be distracted / attacked / your target simply leaves.<br /> The spell takes an action and is subtle as all hell (your eyes flash green, and even that is removable).<br /> <br /> If your storyteller is allowing week-long time-skips during social interaction just to perform a knock-off of Corrupted Words, then <i>there's your problem</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:25:06-07:00","id":1203664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203657#post1203657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lets say for example I make a presence supernal (I did this a few days ago) it might we worth taking a few dots of craft (Painting) to make a few paintings for some subtle social attacks<br /> <br /> On the other hand lets say I make a craft supernal, investing in enough skills to get 5 is multiple forms of craft and harnessing the incredible power of the unconquered sun to allow me to erect cities within days<br /> <br /> Is person one just as much of a crafter as person two?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say a king who is a painter could be a valid description. Maybe not crafter(that term implies a sort of universal skill), but if you were a king who regularly made swords as gifts to your nobles, I'd call you a smith. Maybe not as much as a king, but certainly a smith.<br /> <br /> My disagreement was that knowing sorcerer makes you a sorcerer. Maybe not a skilled or leaned as another sorcerer, but a sorcerer. But in the case of first age artifce, it goes past that.<br /> <br /> In order to dabble in sorcery in order to produce first age artifice, you must have Lore and Occult 5, and be capable of investing significant time into the sorcerous workings of your craft. That sounds a hair more than dabbling.<br /> <br /> I am intreasted, however, in what a non-supplementing sorcerer looks like to you, however. I ahve had the fortune of never dealing with players who lightly took on sorcery, or made it non-essential to their character, so I don't have the best point of veiw on the matter. My antecdotal understanding thinks of sorcerery as just that most of the time: supplemental and expanding the possibilities of a character concept to include stranger and more unuasal facets typically found in charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:26:59-07:00","id":1203665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203660#post1203660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A working costs exp, requires unique ingredients/rituals and takes a week or more to enact during which time you can be distracted / attacked / your target simply leaves.<br /> The spell takes an action and is subtle as all hell (your eyes flash green, and even that is removable).<br /> <br /> If your storyteller is allowing week-long time-skips during social interaction just to perform a knock-off of Corrupted Words, then <i>there's your problem</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>A working costs xp temporarily and while it takes a bit longer it's much more flexible (90% of time your ST will be letting you do it at range","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:45:32-07:00","id":1203678,"title":"","content":"Also, I think comparing a working to an attack spell one uses in combat turns is missing about 99% of the utility and possibilities of sorcerous workings. This isn't D&amp;D where the vast majority of spells are offensive ones used to take down opponents alongside the swordsmen and axe-swinging drwarves in your group. Sorcery is how you get your floating castle, or the gills that let you breathe underwater, or lay a curse on your political enemies' houses down to the seventh generation, or call up a demon who can teach you the secrets of the cosmos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T20:53:39-07:00","id":1203681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203665#post1203665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A working costs xp temporarily and while it takes a bit longer it's much more flexible (90% of time your ST will be letting you do it at range</div> </div> </div> </div>The working costs XP, it doesn\u2019t get refunded unless the workings effect is negated...<br /> <br /> And I think the fundamental disconnect is for you the idea that you can have sorcery without being a sorcerer, that\u2019s not how the system works. Once you have been initiated into sorcery, you are by definition a sorcerer, EVEN if you just dable in sorcery. Sorcerer is an identity that you assume the moment you take up sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","user":"Saipjas","date":". 04-05-2018, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:03:02-07:00","id":1203685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203681#post1203681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The working costs XP, it doesn\u2019t get refunded unless the workings effect is negated...<br /> <br /> And I think the fundamental disconnect is for you the idea that you can have sorcery without being a sorcerer, that\u2019s not how the system works. Once you have been initiated into sorcery, you are by definition a sorcerer, EVEN if you just dable in sorcery. Sorcerer is an identity that you assume the moment you take up sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Generally speaking, and I'm pretty at least one dev has mentioned it, it also applies once the working stops being relevant. Since it does say on page 484 that the xp on a working isn't meant to be a poor investment and also includes mention of a working being made irrelevant being a point where you get the xp back at the end of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:03:52-07:00","id":1203687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203678#post1203678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think comparing a working to an attack spell one uses in combat turns is missing about 99% of the utility and possibilities of sorcerous workings. This isn't D&amp;D where the vast majority of spells are offensive ones used to take down opponents alongside the swordsmen and axe-swinging drwarves in your group. Sorcery is how you get your floating castle, or the gills that let you breathe underwater, or lay a curse on your political enemies' houses down to the seventh generation, or call up a demon who can teach you the secrets of the cosmos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never did that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:05:57-07:00","id":1203689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203681#post1203681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The working costs XP, it doesn\u2019t get refunded unless the workings effect is negated...<br /> <br /> And I think the fundamental disconnect is for you the idea that you can have sorcery without being a sorcerer, that\u2019s not how the system works. Once you have been initiated into sorcery, you are by definition a sorcerer, EVEN if you just dable in sorcery. Sorcerer is an identity that you assume the moment you take up sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>A: What nalak said<br /> B: No","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:08:49-07:00","id":1203692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203685#post1203685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Generally speaking, and I'm pretty at least one dev has mentioned it, it also applies once the working stops being relevant. Since it does say on page 484 that the xp on a working isn't meant to be a poor investment and also includes mention of a working being made irrelevant being a point where you get the xp back at the end of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The examples given there though all involve the destruction of those who were under the effect of the working. I'm not sure how a hypothetical 'curse that replicates corrupted words' working becomes irrelevant in that manner? I mean, if the target dies, but does it still apply if the secret gets out anyway(in which case it's empircally worse than the spell)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:26:17-07:00","id":1203699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203685#post1203685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Generally speaking, and I'm pretty at least one dev has mentioned it, it also applies once the working stops being relevant. Since it does say on page 484 that the xp on a working isn't meant to be a poor investment and also includes mention of a working being made irrelevant being a point where you get the xp back at the end of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s fair, I think I missed that part. @Lion-Hamster I think we will just have to agree to disagree here. You clearly have a set opinion on how you believe sorcery should function and feel that since the game does not support your worldview that there is a disconnect. There have been multiple different people on the thread to try and explain how other interpretations of sorcery make the system valid and usable. So unfortunately since this is something neither of us are going to agree on, I think I\u2019ll bow out of your conversations in this thread. I wish you luck on finding how you can make the system conform to your views.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:50:17-07:00","id":1203707,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11967\" data-vbnamecard=\"11967\">Saipjas</a> Its fairly easy to miss and I wouldn't hold it against an ST who ran it a different way unless they were continually throwing story situations at the PCs that require workings to solve. I mean the method to counter a working is to create another working that makes the first not work, so that would also be an interpretation of a working being made irrelevant. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203692#post1203692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The examples given there though all involve the destruction of those who were under the effect of the working. I'm not sure how a hypothetical 'curse that replicates corrupted words' working becomes irrelevant in that manner? I mean, if the target dies, but does it still apply if the secret gets out anyway(in which case it's empircally worse than the spell)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well those are normal ways to remove a working from play. Honestly, I would say it depends on how one goes about making the working. I mean the way hamster worded it was &quot;draw the breath away from his lungs and draw away his treacherous words&quot; probably wouldn't replicate Corrupted Words. More than likely that working try to suffocate the person anytime they tried to speak with a resulting howling wind that makes it impossible for anyone else to hear what the target says. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:55:15-07:00","id":1203708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203707#post1203707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11967\" data-vbnamecard=\"11967\">Saipjas</a> Its fairly easy to miss and I wouldn't hold it against an ST who ran it a different way unless they were continually throwing story situations at the PCs that require workings to solve. I mean the method to counter a working is to create another working that makes the first not work, so that would also be an interpretation of a working being made irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well those are normal ways to remove a working from play. Honestly, I would say it depends on how one goes about making the working. I mean the way hamster worded it was &quot;draw the breath away from his lungs and draw away his treacherous words&quot; probably wouldn't replicate Corrupted Words. More than likely that working try to suffocate the person anytime they tried to speak with a resulting howling wind that makes it impossible for anyone else to hear what the target says.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure but it is cooler that way isn't it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T22:33:46-07:00","id":1203720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203392#post1203392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIt's a lot more than was ever given in a previous core book.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Black and White Treatise was published nine months later, although obviously that was part of 2e's ridiculously accelerated schedule, and that book itself was clearly an obvious victim of the drawbacks to that sort of approach. But more broadly, yes, obviously nobody could prefer 2e Sorcery.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think that 3e provides much less support for being a spellcaster than it does for any of the other &quot;primary&quot; roles that people are likely to come to the corebook expecting. The issue isn't just the number of spells but the general lack of the concrete sort of progression at spellcasting outside of the three circles - charms build on each other, spells don't.<br /> <br /> If I were revising the 3e core, one of the first changes I'd make would be to remove one or two artifacts and replace them with a full evocation tree for the Talisman of Eyes. It's important. Much, much more important than any one other artifact in the book. Honestly I would go so far as to say that it's more important than all of them - I mean that seriously; if I had to choose between <i>every evocation tree</i> in the 3e core, and the evocation tree for the Talisman of Eyes, I would pick the Talisman in a heartbeat, especially knowing that Arms of the Chosen was going to come out very shortly. Weapon-focused characters can get by on their charms until then; spellcasting-focused characters are essentially incomplete without evocations backing them up because they have no way to really progress at spellcasting outside of accumulating a pile of spells and hitting the limited breakpoints at E3 and E5.<br /> <br /> I think that if the book was like &quot;Yeah, if you want to make a spellcasting-focused character, you're basically Doctor Strange and need a talisman to focus your unique development as a spellcaster&quot;, that would be fine. But right now it just sort of vaguely alludes to this without giving us any real mechanics, and that's a pretty huge failing when it's something huge numbers of players are going to come to a fantasy game like this specifically to play.<br /> <br /> And yes, as you've said, I know there are other facets to playing a Sorcerer than just being a spellcaster, just like there can be more to playing a warrior than just swordsmanship. But I think the fact that these threads come up <i>constantly</i> shows that, yes, the lack of a clear, concrete mechanical way to progress at spellcasting in a satisfying way is as severe of a problem as if the core had been published with an incomplete Solar Melee tree. The other aspects of being a Sorcerer are necessary but not sufficient; different people want different things out of the game, and a lot can be smoothed over having the right group and ST, sure. But &quot;steadily becoming a better spellcaster over time&quot; is still absolutely central to what many people want out of the experience of playing Twilight caste, and absolutely everything in the game's flavor, source material, and marketing says that that's <i>supposed</i> to be something it offers.<br /> <br /> It's failing at it, at least for some people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-06-2018, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T22:38:45-07:00","id":1203725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203720#post1203720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's failing at it, at least for some people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Failing implies it's trying at all, there is nothing there, at all, you get occult at five any you're the best sorcerer you'll ever be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T23:23:10-07:00","id":1203731,"title":"","content":"There's a little bit of support in the Solar charmset. Specifically:<br /> <br /> Spirit-Manifesting Word is very valuable to a summoner, letting you keep a bunch of bound immaterial demons so they don't attract attention, then pull them out for 1m each. Material Exegesis Prana does the same thing on a larger scale.<br /> <br /> Ancient Tongue Understanding boosts your Shape Sorcery rolls, although the disadvantage to activating it is pretty steep.<br /> <br /> Supernal Control Method's full free excellency once per scene helps in the same way and is honestly probably the best Sorcery-boosting charm Solars get aside from Spirit Drawing Oculus.<br /> <br /> Spirit-Draining Mudra can be used to power your spells, although it's often a pain in the ass to set it up when you need it.<br /> <br /> Spirit Drawing Oculus can be used to power spells, too, and is probably the best Sorcery-boosting charm Solars have. A free mote reserve for shaping actions is a pretty big deal.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's a few Craft charms that could be relevant.<br /> <br /> Breach-Healing Method creates an aura that grants a non-charm dice bonus equal to your Essence to several things, including Occult rolls (and therefore Shape Sorcery rolls), as long as you are working on repairing an object or treating an injury. I do not believe this is the charm's intent, but technically you are inside your own aura and can benefit from the bonus yourself when shaping spells to accomplish those things - it says the Solar &quot;establishes a field&quot; and grants the bonuses to &quot;anyone standing in this field&quot;, not &quot;anyone ELSE standing in this field&quot;. The text at the very end mentioning how you inspire those around you could be interpreted as explaining why the bonus <i>also</i> affects others rather than limiting the bonus to others.<br /> <br /> Words-as-Workshop Method can be used to summon Occult-boosting artifacts like the Talisman of Eyes (and you explicitly get their evocations for free - seriously, that charm is INSANE. I don't get why people don't discuss it more.) Unfortunately we have no idea what those artifacts look like.<br /> <br /> But my problem with these is that they don't really provide a way to develop your spellcasting in any concrete direction, outside of <i>maybe</i> &quot;generic summoner&quot;, which everyone who uses Sorcery already is because it's so good (ironically, Breach-Healing Method, using the &quot;inside-my-own-field&quot; interpretation I suggested above, is actually the closest we have, since it makes you better at using sorcery to heal or repair stuff specifically.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-06-2018, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T23:30:50-07:00","id":1203732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203731#post1203731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Breach-Healing Method creates an aura that grants a non-charm dice bonus equal to your Essence to several things, including Occult rolls (and therefore Shape Sorcery rolls), as long as you are working on repairing an object or treating an injury. I do not believe this is the charm's intent, but technically you are inside your own aura and can benefit from the bonus yourself when shaping spells to accomplish those things - it says the Solar &quot;establishes a field&quot; and grants the bonuses to &quot;anyone standing in this field&quot;, not &quot;anyone ELSE standing in this field&quot;. The text at the very end mentioning how you inspire those around you could be interpreted as explaining why the bonus <i>also</i> affects others rather than limiting the bonus to others.<br /> <br /> Words-as-Workshop Method can be used to summon Occult-boosting artifacts like the Talisman of Eyes, for instance (and you explicitly get their evocations for free - seriously, that charm is INSANE. I don't get why people don't discuss it more.) Unfortunately we have no idea what those artifacts look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Craft charms... seriously","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T23:51:36-07:00","id":1203737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203732#post1203732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craft charms... seriously</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T00:42:43-07:00","id":1203745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203737#post1203737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, you see. You CANNOT have charms on an Ability complementing charms on another Ability. That\u00b4s a blasphemy on the eyes of Glorious Sol. If you have charms useful for sorcery on another ability, like Craft, or Lore, that is not Occult, the game is broken.<br /> <br /> Or something. I have had players using magic, and they felt mythic and cool. The magic didn\u00b4t define them, but it was a part of their concept. One was a sorcerer-queen, an intriguing noble using whatever means she can to keep her siblings and the other nobles and kingdoms in line, including sorcery, which she used a lot in her intrigues (Corrupted Words and that spell that allows you to socially influence people on their dreams were massively useful, along Summon Demon of the First Circle, to use as invisible spies and thiefs, picking the personal items she needed for her sorceries), the other was a pirate-adventurer on the Dreaming Sea, a philosopher and scholar, practicing both alchemy and sorcery in his quest to personal and spiritual trascendence. He mainly uses summoning for spies, henchmen, communication or travel, Disguise of the New Face for infiltration purposes (he once &quot;stole&quot; a body, picking a Navy officer appearance, and giving her his appearance, so he could infiltratein her garrison), and sorcerous workings, like the one he is trying to do right now, to &quot;calcify&quot; his Fae slave, melting it with his ship, making it all weird and stuff, with strange powers and stuff. His magic came from a Fae Lord he served, &quot;gifting&quot; him with madness, from which confused dreams he has gotten the means for mystic understanding.<br /> <br /> I think both are pretty mythic, and would be hard to say they are not sorcerers. In fact, I think that if they are not sorcerers, I don\u00b4t want to meet any sorcerer, they probably aren\u00b4t very interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T00:50:07-07:00","id":1203747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203745#post1203745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you see. You CANNOT have charms on an Ability complementing charms on another Ability. That\u00b4s a blasphemy on the eyes of Glorious Sol. If you have charms useful for sorcery on another ability, like Craft, or Lore, that is not Occult, the game is broken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, needing to go between 3 different skills to get good at something when you have a mechanic like supernals is bad game design, yes, particularly when it's the only mechanic for which that's necessary","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T00:57:24-07:00","id":1203749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203732#post1203732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craft charms... seriously</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... Words-as-Workshop Method is just insane (depending on how permissive your ST is, it's not only the best Craft charm, but also the best Medicine, Lore, Occult, and Investigation charm. I could very easily see that one charm, on its own, sometimes making you more effective at healing people than every single published Solar Medicine charm - though obviously you'd be even better with both. &quot;Here's an artifact specialized just for curing this disease, with its entire massive evocation tree unlocked&quot; is hard to compete with.)<br /> <br /> But Breach-Healing Method is reasonable? It's a Craft charm that makes you better at using Sorcery for a craft-related task (repairing stuff, although also healing people for some reason), so it sits at the intersection of the two abilities. Charms like that are good to have because they help make a Twilight a better sorcerer than eg. a Dawn who favored Occult.<br /> <br /> The synergy between stuff like Stealth and Larceny or between Resistance and Melee is obvious, but the synergy between some of the Twilight abilities is worth specifically working into the charms and mechanics to ensure that the caste retains cohesion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203747#post1203747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, needing to go between 3 different skills to get good at something when you have a mechanic like supernals is bad game design, yes, particularly when it's the only mechanic for which that's necessary</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it shouldn't be <i>necessary</i>. But it's nice to have synergies like that available for Twilights who are already in both those abilities (as many Twilights would be expected to be.)<br /> <br /> Again, this helps differentiate the Twilight who mastered both Craft and Occult from the Dawn who just picked up one of them.<br /> <br /> Like I said above, I mostly agree with you, but I wouldn't want to see that aspect of Breach-Healing Method go away. &quot;I'm so good at fixing stuff that I get a bonus to using Sorcery to fix stuff&quot; is a reasonable charm in Craft, especially with both Craft and Occult falling under the same caste.<br /> <br /> (Words-as-Workshop Method is something else. It is definitely a very <i>fun</i> charm as long as you have an understanding with your ST and don't abuse it, at least. And let's be real, Craft needs that charm - amid a sea of &quot;fiddle with this number slightly&quot;, its ridiculous thematic of &quot;yeah, just pull whatever power you need to resolve your current situation out of your ass&quot; sort of stands out.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-06-2018, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T01:10:26-07:00","id":1203751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203749#post1203749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... Words-as-Workshop Method is just insane (depending on how permissive your ST is, it's not only the best Craft charm, but also the best Medicine, Lore, Occult, and Investigation charm. I could very easily see that one charm, on its own, sometimes making you more effective at healing people than every single published Solar Medicine charm - though obviously you'd be even better with both. &quot;Here's an artifact specialized just for curing this disease, with its entire massive evocation tree unlocked&quot; is hard to compete with.)<br /> <br /> But Breach-Healing Method is reasonable? It's a Craft charm that makes you better at using Sorcery for a craft-related task (repairing stuff, although also healing people for some reason), so it sits at the intersection of the two abilities. Charms like that are good to have because they help make a Twilight a better sorcerer than eg. a Dawn who favored Occult.<br /> <br /> The synergy between stuff like Stealth and Larceny or between Resistance and Melee is obvious, but the synergy between some of the Twilight abilities is worth specifically working into the charms and mechanics to ensure that the caste retains cohesion.<br /> <br /> Well, it shouldn't be <i>necessary</i>. But it's nice to have synergies like that available for Twilights who are already in both those abilities (as many Twilights would be expected to be.)<br /> <br /> Again, this helps differentiate the Twilight who mastered both Craft and Occult from the Dawn who just picked up one of them.<br /> <br /> Like I said above, I mostly agree with you, but I wouldn't want to see that aspect of Breach-Healing Method go away. &quot;I'm so good at fixing stuff that I get a bonus to using Sorcery to fix stuff&quot; is a reasonable charm in Craft, especially with both Craft and Occult falling under the same caste.<br /> <br /> (Words-as-Workshop Method is something else. It is definitely a very <i>fun</i> charm as long as you have an understanding with your ST and don't abuse it, at least. And let's be real, Craft needs that charm - amid a sea of &quot;fiddle with this number slightly&quot;, its ridiculous thematic of &quot;yeah, just pull whatever power you need to resolve your current situation out of your ass&quot; sort of stands out.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's fine for there to be synergy charms but when the list of charms that help with sorcery can be counted on your fingers having to go cross-skill for 2 of them is a little much, they sound like great charms but it seems like a insult to injury deal<br /> <br /> Addendum: Words as workshop is awesome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23635,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","user":"Lion Hamster","date":".  Read words as workshop 04-06-2018, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T01:42:44-07:00","id":1203756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203747#post1203747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, needing to go between 3 different skills to get good at something when you have a mechanic like supernals is bad game design, yes, particularly when it's the only mechanic for which that's necessary</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure the poster you quoted was employing sarcasm. <br /> <br /> Abilities are <i>supposed to </i>complement one another. The Melee 5 guy with Awareness 5 is almost always going to fare better in swordfights than the guy with just Melee 5. The guy with both Abilities <i>and Resistance</i> at 5 will probably fare even better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-06-2018, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T01:57:27-07:00","id":1203760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203756#post1203756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure the poster you quoted was employing sarcasm.<br /> <br /> Abilities are <i>supposed to </i>complement one another. The Melee 5 guy with Awareness 5 is almost always going to fare better in swordfights than the guy with just Melee 5. The guy with both Abilities <i>and Resistance</i> at 5 will probably fare even better.</div> </div> </div> </div>A: I knew that<br /> B: It's one thing if the guy with a bunch of melee charms isn't as good as a guy with a bunch of melee charms AND awareness but having the best melee charms be in dodge is another thing entirely","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T02:06:10-07:00","id":1203765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203751#post1203751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Addendum: Words as workshop is awesome</div> </div> </div> </div>It really is. I don't get why people don't talk about it more. Like... people were complaining about Dual Magus Prana or God King's Shrike, charms that almost never come up, while Words as Workshop Method lets you instantly produce a ridiculous amount of specialized power for just about any task within the classic Twilight ability spread. And let's be real, almost anything can be turned into a Craft, Lore or Occult task if you're creative enough.<br /> <br /> (eg. &quot;I want to use my vast knowledge of lore to put together a perfect plan to accomplish X, and I'm going to create a Path-to-Victory crystal to help me determine the best way to do it.&quot; Although my favorite is &quot;I want to make that city's walls collapse, as a craft action. Words as Workshop Method for a beam-cannon that knocks over walls.&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T02:13:34-07:00","id":1203766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203765#post1203765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really is. I don't get why people don't talk about it more. Like... people were complaining about Dual Magus Prana or God King's Shrike, charms that almost never come up, while Words as Workshop Method lets you instantly produce a ridiculous amount of specialized power for just about any task within the classic Twilight ability spread. And let's be real, almost anything can be turned into a Craft, Lore or Occult task if you're creative enough.<br /> <br /> (eg. &quot;I want to use my vast knowledge of lore to put together a perfect plan to accomplish X, and I'm going to create a Path-to-Victory crystal to help me determine the best way to do it.&quot; Although my favorite is &quot;I want to make that city's walls collapse, as a craft action. Words as Workshop Method for a beam-cannon that knocks over walls.&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I just think the idea of pinning a persons soul to their body while performing surgery on someone to be awesome, though I suppose that's probably the least you can do with that charm, kinda a shame that's in crafting though considering it's clearly the best everything charm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T03:24:03-07:00","id":1203774,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Jesus, this goes on for two more pages of the same roundabout goalposts and obtuse talking points? Oyyy not worth it.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b... Okay, maybe just one:</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203654#post1203654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The ability to replicate it with a working, while you could permanently spend 10xp to learn corrupted words, you can use a terrestrial circle working to &quot;Take the breath from his lungs and draw away his treacherous words&quot; while there may well be a circumstance where it's worth it 10xp is a hell of a lot for <b>something that <i>might</i> come in handy eventually</b></span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Jesus Christ, if nothing else (and seriously, how is there nothing else in a game expected to have enough social interaction focused scenes to have three or four Abilities about it), you have the latitude to seek those situations out.<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, workings provide a method of binding somebody's tongue if you only ever expect to do that once, but if you can't figure out the utility of that kind of power to see the benefit of having it more reliably and consistently, that's on you.<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Aquillion, I think progression in sorcery is better off being something that moves laterally into being able to do a greater variety of eclectic things rather than expanding vertically, for reasons including that it has to be a form of magic that competes effectively with the magic that pretty much everybody that is going to learn it can already use, without risk of superseding them entirely.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bI mean, maybe in previous Editions it could have covered a niche of providing forms of power not native to an Exalt, but Evocations are doing that now, and I think they're better suited for reasons that start with each path being tied to a single object.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Speaking of which.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203720#post1203720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If I were revising the 3e core, one of the first changes I'd make would be to remove one or two artifacts and replace them with a full evocation tree for the Talisman of Eyes. It's important. Much, much more important than any one other artifact in the book. Honestly I would go so far as to say that it's more important than all of them - I mean that seriously; if I had to choose between <i>every evocation tree</i> in the 3e core, and the evocation tree for the Talisman of Eyes, I would pick the Talisman in a heartbeat, especially knowing that Arms of the Chosen was going to come out very shortly.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bIt's clearly important to <i>you</i>, but I don't think it's necessarily the highest priority in the corebook.</span></span></span></div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T03:58:40-07:00","id":1203782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203774#post1203774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aquillion, I think progression in sorcery is better off being something that moves laterally into being able to do a greater variety of eclectic things rather than expanding vertically, for reasons including that it has to be a form of magic that competes effectively with the magic that pretty much everybody that is going to learn it can already use, without risk of superseding them entirely</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember linear fighter exponential wizard?<br /> You're suggesting linear fighter flat wizard (Well, more like exponential fighter flat wizard but same difference)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23635,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","user":"Lion Hamster","date":". 04-06-2018, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T04:09:47-07:00","id":1203784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203782#post1203782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember linear fighter exponential wizard?<br /> You're suggesting linear fighter flat wizard (Well, more like exponential fighter flat wizard but same difference)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSee, one thing that is definitely necessary in any assessment of Exalted sorcerers, whether the sorcery is intended to be a central focus of the characters or not, is that they are in no way equivalent to any Dungeons and Dragons class, because even if it's highly unlikely that any single character could encompass the entire Solar Charm set, plus sorcery, plus Martial Arts, no character is particularly barred from any of those things, so they can be mixed and matched in a variety of ways.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat was part of my point with why sorcery needs to be reconciled with Charms; the expectation that just about any sorcerer character will have a decent mix of both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T04:13:14-07:00","id":1203785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203784#post1203784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSee, one thing that is definitely necessary in any assessment of Exalted sorcerers, whether the sorcery is intended to be a central focus of the characters or not, is that they are in no way equivalent to any Dungeons and Dragons class, because even if it's highly unlikely that any single character could encompass the entire Solar Charm set, plus sorcery, plus Martial Arts, no character is particularly barred from any of those things, so they can be mixed and matched in a variety of ways.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat was part of my point with why sorcery needs to be reconciled with Charms; the expectation that just about any sorcerer character will have a decent mix of both.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right about one thing dnd wizards are nothing like exalted sorcerers, dnd wizards are actually good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T05:12:26-07:00","id":1203792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203785#post1203785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right about one thing dnd wizards are nothing like exalted sorcerers, dnd wizards are actually good</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is an entirely ridiculous statement. The level of difference between Exalted fighters and sorcerers mechanically speaking is nothing like the difference between you're 3rd level D&amp;D fighter and a 3rd level wizard who knows how to use Rope Trick in 3.5. D&amp;D spellcasters are perhaps the worst example to draw from within <i>any </i>TTRPG because of how stupidly abusive their capabilities are compared to character classes focused on &quot;mundane&quot; abilities.<br /> <br /> Instead, why not take a look at the GURPS spellcasting rules in their 4th edition core set, which is another crunchy system including magic. Not only did your character have to buy an advantage to have magical aptitude, you also had to purchase each individual magic spell as a difficult-to-learn skill. Without some serious setting work by a GM, GURPS spellcasters often end up being more like skill monkeys with very strange abilities that require player creativity to effectively employ. While still distant from Exalted's treatment of sorcery, it's much closer than the wizards and clerics of D&amp;D with mechanical abilities that invalidate the rest of the system and most intuitive game premises.<br /> <br /> I agree on the the fact that there aren't very many charms out there that improve sorcery in the Solar charmset (perhaps because their is an emphasis on making Solar characters unique based on their charm trees instead of a mechanic shared with other exalts). There's also nothing in the rules that says you can't make custom charms adding dice tricks to shape sorcery actions like many melee charms do. There's also nothing out there in the rules that says you can't have an artifact with evocations that aid in sorcery. If you want your game to have sorcery work more like melee (or even better than it), than try your hand at writing those charms, evocations, and maybe even new spells. Exalted seems to have always been a game that essentially relies on the players to write up mechanics, for better or for worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio","name":"Houlio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T05:17:50-07:00","id":1203793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Houlio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203792#post1203792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is an entirely ridiculous statement. The level of difference between Exalted fighters and sorcerers mechanically speaking is nothing like the difference between you're 3rd level D&amp;D fighter and a 3rd level wizard who knows how to use Rope Trick in 3.5. D&amp;D spellcasters are perhaps the worst example to draw from within <i>any </i>TTRPG because of how stupidly abusive their capabilities are compared to character classes focused on &quot;mundane&quot; abilities.<br /> <br /> Instead, why not take a look at the GURPS spellcasting rules in their 4th edition core set, which is another crunchy system including magic. Not only did your character have to buy an advantage to have magical aptitude, you also had to purchase each individual magic spell as a difficult-to-learn skill. Without some serious setting work by a GM, GURPS spellcasters often end up being more like skill monkeys with very strange abilities that require player creativity to effectively employ. While still distant from Exalted's treatment of sorcery, it's much closer than the wizards and clerics of D&amp;D with mechanical abilities that invalidate the rest of the system and most intuitive game premises.<br /> <br /> I agree on the the fact that there aren't very many charms out there that improve sorcery in the Solar charmset (perhaps because their is an emphasis on making Solar characters unique based on their charm trees instead of a mechanic shared with other exalts). There's also nothing in the rules that says you can't make custom charms adding dice tricks to shape sorcery actions like many melee charms do. There's also nothing out there in the rules that says you can't have an artifact with evocations that aid in sorcery. If you want your game to have sorcery work more like melee (or even better than it), than try your hand at writing those charms, evocations, and maybe even new spells. Exalted seems to have always been a game that essentially relies on the players to write up mechanics, for better or for worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a system for custom charms doesn't justify making a shitty charm tree, when there is a complete lack of charms for something like this it's rather hard to justify it, if lore didn't have any charms for fact introduction or brawl for grappling you have a problem, realistically custom charms shouldn't be used to make an entire charm sub-tree, they should be used to add one or two charms to perform a feat core to their legend","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T06:22:15-07:00","id":1203802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203707#post1203707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11967\" data-vbnamecard=\"11967\">Saipjas</a> Its fairly easy to miss and I wouldn't hold it against an ST who ran it a different way unless they were continually throwing story situations at the PCs that require workings to solve. I mean the method to counter a working is to create another working that makes the first not work, so that would also be an interpretation of a working being made irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well those are normal ways to remove a working from play. Honestly, I would say it depends on how one goes about making the working. I mean the way hamster worded it was &quot;draw the breath away from his lungs and draw away his treacherous words&quot; probably wouldn't replicate Corrupted Words. More than likely that working try to suffocate the person anytime they tried to speak with a resulting howling wind that makes it impossible for anyone else to hear what the target says.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My necromancer made a magical plague that only affected devouts of a certain god, as a bargaining chip to get him to fall in line. When it was clear the working was no longer necessary I countered the working myself, and got the exp back.<br /> We also used sorcery to replace a couple missing limbs inflicted during a bloody battle against a behemoth, and when our medic reaches essence 3 those will also be refunded via &quot;I grow my arm back&quot; medicine.<br /> <br /> So yeah, there are ways to be refunded the working that don't involve it being *destroyed* or *countered*. Anything that makes it obsolete goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T06:25:12-07:00","id":1203803,"title":"","content":"I believe there has been some talk of Charms to interact with sorcery with the Dragon Blooded, so I'll be interested to see any insights that may be provided there. I feel as though it's a subject fraught enough, especially with regards to workings, to have had reservations about pursuing it. Not to mention a desire to build Solar Occult as its own thing, rather than give a sense that it was solely about sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T06:36:57-07:00","id":1203805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203793#post1203793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having a system for custom charms doesn't justify making a shitty charm tree, when there is a complete lack of charms for something like this it's rather hard to justify it, if lore didn't have any charms for fact introduction or brawl for grappling you have a problem, realistically custom charms shouldn't be used to make an entire charm sub-tree, they should be used to add one or two charms to perform a feat core to their legend</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I also think Occult is a shitty tree that requires your ST to give you the appropriate game, although not quite like Sail.<br /> <br /> Although there isn't as many charms as I would like to see about sorcery (and I also think it's unfortunately skimped on), you're being hyperbolic when you say that there is a complete lack of charms in Occult to support sorcery. By investing in one other charm which also aids Occult rolls, you can grab a 1/scene full free occult excellency, and if that isn't designed for sorcery I don't know what is. That said, while there is sorcery support in Occult, it's kinda all over the place and requires a character to probably grab a lot of charms involving spirits they might not otherwise want.<br /> <br /> Also, the way mechanics have been made for Ex3 means that it isn't all that hard to fill out a charm tree at E1 and E2 with dice tricks. At around E3 is where the really big and resounding effects occur. Writing exactly one or two charms for your sorcerer (who already is supposed to be rather unique via shaping rituals) isn't that ridiculous. Charms at E4 and E5 tend to focus on improving the real flashy stuff at E3 in different ways.<br /> <br /> Do I wish there was better sorcery support in Occult? Oh yeah.<br /> Is sorcery pointless without it? Hell no.<br /> <br /> Is it annoying, and in some ways disappointing, to be expected to write mechanics for a game? Of course.<br /> Am I angry that Melee has some cool subtrees over more sorcery-related charms? No, writing up some basic charms for sorcery akin to Excellent Strike or Rising Sun Slash doesn't seem overly difficult. Writing something like Peony-Blossom Technique seems really hard for someone without a lot of design thought and play-testing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12226-houlio","name":"Houlio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T08:07:17-07:00","id":1203835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203429#post1203429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my friend is playing a sorceress.<br /> She rules a kingdom of fanatically loyal, 6 1/2 foot people many of whom have some fire magick. They have multiple dragons, hundreds of gryffons and golems. Their mountain kingdom is magically fertile so produces tons of food.<br /> She also has fiery wings she can summon at will, strange viscous fire-blood, jet-black skin with burning white veins, and a heart of fire.<br /> <br /> Oh, also her kingdom has a giant demon-built canal through it.<br /> <br /> All of this she did with sorcery. It seems pretty dramatic and life-altering to me.<br /> <br /> Another friend of mine plays a sorcerer who lives in a giant flying castle with its own sun (which, again, he made with sorcery).<br /> <br /> Now, sure, there are far less spells than charms in the book. But you can do tons with workings. And as Isator said, there's more spells than in the Core for 3rd ed than for 2nd. Yes, we could do with more spells... but hey, a Solar sorcerer at least has some spells. Lunars and Sidereals don't even have any charms!<br /> <br /> Admittedly, a couple of others got like one spell when they were high-XP, but it's not really surprising that when you start going into a new area when you've already got 300xp, it's not a big part of your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question. How long did it take to make all that in game time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T08:21:04-07:00","id":1203842,"title":"","content":"Well, she did a couple of things close together, then like a year later she did another bunch of stuff over about 6 months maybe, and then over the next six months she made the kingdom magically fertile.<br /> So, about a year and a half to two years, but she was adventuring in between stuff (killing thousands of horse nomads with Death Ray, ripping DBs to bits with Obsidian Butterflies, and other un-sorcery related stuff).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-06-2018, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T08:47:42-07:00","id":1203853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203626#post1203626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lore charm gives 5 bonus die here, bringing us to 26-28 die, adding 2 expected successes per roll, for a total of 55~ successes w/o means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heaven-Turning Calculuations does not apply to Workings. The closest thing it does is apply to &quot;Spell Effects&quot;. Workings are not spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Here's an artifact specialized just for curing this disease, with its entire massive evocation tree unlocked&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason to think and no suggestion in the text that Words-As-Workshop unlocks evocations. There's even a suggestion for the effect: &quot;A couple non-charm dice&quot;. I would think that most effects you get out of Words-As-Workshop would be in line with that, and when the best working-boosting charm in the game is Six Eternities Travail, compared to something like Any Craft Charm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","user":"nihnoz","date":". 04-06-2018, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:30:06-07:00","id":1203863,"title":"","content":"If I can chime in here, with a slightly different perspective...<br /> <br /> I agree with Lion Hamser's premise - in the setting, sorcery is supposed to entirely change your identity or outlook in some way. The rules as written do very little to enforce this, because sorcery as written is a minimal investment. You buy your circles, and you can be a sorcerer. Hell, from an efficiency point of view there's very little reason for every Exalt ever not to take Terrestrial - you get a spell (charm equivalent), the ability to make workings, and a shaping ritual. That's a lot of bang for your buck.<br /> <br /> And then... that's as far as the system goes. It feels like Exalted, as a relatively crunchy system, tends to veer towards those elements of the game that have more mechanics to them. This means that charms get the lion's share of many character considerations. Sorcery, being mechanically a few things like charms (spells) plus a structured system for storyteller fiat/homebrew (workings), really doesn't. And so that leaves characters which dip into sorcery alongside other concepts, as they don't have much room within the system to expand any sorcery-based concepts.<br /> <br /> I think the comparison with D&amp;D is warranted, not because of spells, but (from what I remember about 3.5E) with skills. Both fighters and magic users get points to spend on skills. How these are spent would look quite different. In Exalted, a sorcerer's charm spread will have the Circle charms and maybe a few utility charms here and there to help with casting and/or workings, but will be maybe 2/3 the same as a similar concept without sorcery. That's what I see with this system, having ST'd in stories with sorcerer characters who were:<ul><li>Rurouni Kenshin with sorcery</li> <li>Street-fighting smith with sorcery</li> <li>Alchemical scholar/teacher with sorcery</li> <li>Slavery rebellion leader with sorcery</li> </ul>Of these, only the scholar felt at all like a sorcerer is portrayed in the background, because the rest could easily dip in for a grab-bag of assorted abilities for one charm pick, and focus their key abilities in other areas. Exalted's system just doesn't support the conceptual character depth for sorcerers that its setting describes.<br /> <br /> One possible patch for this, now I think about it, is to mandate that each sorcerer take a defining intimacy to do with their sorcerous abilities; maybe a tie to the object of their initiation, a principle that was introduced to them through their shaping ritual, something to do with how they've been treated by others subsequent to becoming a sorcerer. For each circle they advance in, they need to take a new Defining (or maybe Major for the second and third?) Intimacy. That feels like it may give the character's involvement and the &quot;shift in perspective&quot; that supposed to be part and parcel of the sorcery experience a bit more weight, with the minimal in system reworking.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:42:16-07:00","id":1203868,"title":"","content":"The bulk of the systemic transformation there is in the initiations themselves, which you seem to only give minor consideration.<br /> Look at them, closely, along with the merits and rituals they bring forth. The simplest, least disruptive ones (pact with efreet, talisman...) still determine part of your outlook on the world, giving you preternatural awareness or changing your very body such that you embrace fire in ways that outright kill most people. If that doesn't give you an alien perspective, I don't know what does.<br /> <br /> And then you get into ascetics, miraculous madmen, soul eaters. And that's all before even considering a prime element of sorcery in exalted: the prominence of supernatural servants, especially demons.<br /> <br /> And you're telling me that's meaningless? That those things don't make a person different from their own people? A dabbler is clearly less of an obvious sorcerer than a full sorcerer, but can you truly say that someone that makes love to fire to get their spells going, even just a dabbler, is nearly indistinct from a non-sorcerer?<br /> Now factor in workings and how they are made, how they change the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>You</b> are downplaying sorcery, reducing the entire significance of sorcery to &quot;get this charm&quot; just because when you look at a number on a sheet that's what it costs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T09:54:04-07:00","id":1203875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203863#post1203863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in the setting, sorcery is supposed to entirely change your identity or outlook in some way. The rules as written do very little to enforce this</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, like Essence fever.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, I imagine that if you've initiated into sorcery via a method that allows you to drain people's souls and turn it into motes, that might be expected to affect your outlook and validate people being a bit squirrelly around you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 04-06-2018, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T11:20:34-07:00","id":1203909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203868#post1203868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bulk of the systemic transformation there is in the initiations themselves, which you seem to only give minor consideration.<br /> Look at them, closely, along with the merits and rituals they bring forth. The simplest, least disruptive ones (pact with efreet, talisman...) still determine part of your outlook on the world, giving you preternatural awareness or changing your very body such that you embrace fire in ways that outright kill most people. If that doesn't give you an alien perspective, I don't know what does.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, the merits are an element I overlooked. The book, however, seems to do something similar - they're tucked away at the back, with no signposting in either the Circle charms or the Merits section that they exist. So they're also very easy to overlook when designing a character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203868#post1203868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you're telling me that's meaningless? That those things don't make a person different from their own people?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I'm saying that the rules don't make all that mind-altering stuff matter as much as stuff that is relatively mundane (charms), because of the relative system weight behind each system. The rules for sorcery do not make you think that having sorcery makes a character different; it functions like a relatively low cost ability to buy into. And because of that low cost, despite all the flavour complexity, my players have bought into it on that level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203868#post1203868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>You</b> are downplaying sorcery, reducing the entire significance of sorcery to &quot;get this charm&quot; just because when you look at a number on a sheet that's what it costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not done this. I have explained to my players what sorcery is, and what it means. I've been presented with the examples that I presented above, most of which treat it as a tacked-on element because the weight the flavour gives it is different between the weight that the system does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T11:33:45-07:00","id":1203914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203909#post1203909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not done this. I have explained to my players what sorcery is, and what it means. I've been presented with the examples that I presented above, most of which treat it as a tacked-on element because the weight the flavour gives it is different between the weight that the system does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extend that <b>you</b> to your players. The mistake being committed there is attaching the experience costs to the weight of the narrative is not exactly the wisest thing. I'm all for advocating a system that encourages you to play in a certain way, which the initiations <b>do</b>. The counterpart to that is the system being heavy such that to be a sorcerer you can't afford anything that doesn't complement it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T11:42:03-07:00","id":1203916,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm... Yeah, I kind of agree with Xerxes. I mean, I don't want to, but I kind of do.<br /> <br /> For the players that said &quot;I'm going to play a sorcerer&quot;, sorcery has been a dramatic transformation in their characters' backstories. For example, the sorceress I mentioned originally made a pact with an ancient and dark fire spirit, giving her various strange mutations, fire magick, and leading her to build him a giant temple. It's a very significant part of her character, so much so that she's known far more as &quot;the dragon-riding fire-sorceress of the mountains&quot; than &quot;a Solar.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the other hand, for the people who just bought one spell when they were already at over 300xp... it hasn't changed their characters much at all. I'd argue this is partially because they didn't want it to change their character much though. So, I suppose the question is, do we want a system that forces your character to change dramatically when you buy into it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T11:52:02-07:00","id":1203919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203916#post1203916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm... Yeah, I kind of agree with Xerxes. I mean, I don't want to, but I kind of do.<br /> <br /> For the players that said &amp;quot;I'm going to play a sorcerer&amp;quot;, sorcery has been a dramatic transformation in their characters' backstories. For example, the sorceress I mentioned originally made a pact with an ancient and dark fire spirit, giving her various strange mutations, fire magick, and leading her to build him a giant temple. It's a very significant part of her character, so much so that she's known far more as &amp;quot;the dragon-riding fire-sorceress of the mountains&amp;quot; than &amp;quot;a Solar.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> On the other hand, for the people who just bought one spell when they were already at over 300xp... it hasn't changed their characters much at all. I'd argue this is partially because they didn't want it to change their character much though. So, I suppose the question is, do we want a system that forces your character to change dramatically when you buy into it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the transformative occurs THROUGH the initiation ritual. \u201cBuying a spell\u201d is not a thing that occurs, you buy a charm which gives you a spell, AND initiates you into sorcery through (insert transformative ritual). <br /> <br /> One of my pushbacks is that there is not really such a thing as \u201cdabbling\u201d because initiating into sorcery makes you a sorcerer, whether you want it to be an identity of your character or not. It\u2019s like saying a person who initiated in MA to \u201cdabble\u201d is not a martial artist.<br /> <br /> The paradigm that the core is trying to tell is not inline with the idea that sorcery is an act rather than a state of being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T11:56:42-07:00","id":1203926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203909#post1203909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, the merits are an element I overlooked. The book, however, seems to do something similar - they're tucked away at the back, with no signposting in either the Circle charms or the Merits section that they exist. So they're also very easy to overlook when designing a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGod knows that nobody who wants to design a character with sorcery is going to look in the chapter with &quot;sorcery&quot; in its title.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou know what, I've just realised that Martial Arts are terrible as well because they're not put in the setting chapter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T12:27:33-07:00","id":1203942,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I found them pretty easy to find. And cool. Though the formatting could have made them stand out a bit more.<br /> <br /> Possibly there was the thing that the initiations were all new and dramatic whereas most of the spells were ones I'd seen before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T13:07:49-07:00","id":1203963,"title":"","content":"A thing of note.* Exalts only have to buy a charm to gain access to sorcery, but mortals need to acquire a 5 dot merit to get their first shaping ritual. (core pg 470)** Considering Sorcery is described in part as learning to feel and wield the essence of the world. Exalts are already used to wielding essence, so sorcery being wielding power that is entirely external to them might be weird, but its more extreme for a mortal to deal with than an Exalt.<br /> <br /> *I mean there's always the thing that if the player doesn't want to play having access to sorcery as anything more than another tool in their belt that's how its going to be, but this might be of note.<br /> <br /> ** Yes I know merits are not a distinct thing in universe, but the dots tend to describe how powerful ,and consequently impactful, said merit is on a character that possesses it. So that getting a shaping ritual for a mortal is a 5 dot merit is probably not a small means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T13:12:51-07:00","id":1203965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203919#post1203919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except the transformative occurs THROUGH the initiation ritual. \u201cBuying a spell\u201d is not a thing that occurs, you buy a charm which gives you a spell, AND initiates you into sorcery through (insert transformative ritual).<br /> <br /> One of my pushbacks is that there is not really such a thing as \u201cdabbling\u201d because initiating into sorcery makes you a sorcerer, whether you want it to be an identity of your character or not. It\u2019s like saying a person who initiated in MA to \u201cdabble\u201d is not a martial artist.<br /> <br /> The paradigm that the core is trying to tell is not inline with the idea that sorcery is an act rather than a state of being.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the paradigm the core is trying to tell is not backed up by the game system. It does not make you look through the act of character creation through the lens of sorcery, like the setting feels like it should.<br /> <br /> The comparison to martial arts doesn't work. To get martial arts, you need to buy a 3 point merit, assign ability dots to an ability used for nothing else, and then pump lots of individual charms into it. The system makes you invest in it. The system for sorcery makes you buy one charm, choose a shaping ritual and control spell, and that's it. No additional investment required. It doesn't shift the focus of the character unless the player intentionally designs it that way. Which many do, I'm sure, but the system makes incidental sorcery very easy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203926#post1203926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bGod knows that nobody who wants to design a character with sorcery is going to look in the chapter with &quot;sorcery&quot; in its title.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou know what, I've just realised that Martial Arts are terrible as well because they're not put in the setting chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay for snark.<br /> <br /> Part of my current issue may be my players. Two I'm fairly certain have learning difficulties, and for one of those choosing Linguistics and Lore charms (resulting in 5 picks) took over an hour. These are not the kind of people who will read and retain large blocks of text in a 600+ page book when stuff in the sections they do read does not signpost them that they need to do that. I'm aware that's part of my job as ST, in which case I probably suck at it, but having some suggestions of what options sorcery opens up in terms of spending points on it the section that talks about spending points would have helped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T13:20:10-07:00","id":1203970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203642#post1203642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core book didn't even give us a single evocation tree to progress along, it just vaguely implied it exists. If your Sorcerer knows a thousand spells, there is still absolutely no incentive for you to pick up your thousand-and-first spell rather than buying a Melee charm to balance things out (and in practice, since you grab the best spells first, it's less &quot;a thousand spells&quot; and more &quot;two or three spells.&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is mostly a symptom of insufficient/wonkily balanced spells. If melee charms had no prerequisites and you could jump around grabbing whichever ones you liked at any moment, I would still make characters who dump all their XP on grabbing dozens of different melee charms because they do a lot of different and very powerful things, and my character who has all the melee charms would feel awesome compared to people who've just dipped for two or three of the best charms. Admittedly this isn't a perfect comparison because charms combine much more easily than spells do, but while I agree that right now it's &quot;grab demon of the Xth circle, grab stormwind rider, maybe get something else for flavour&quot;, if there were as many potent and game-changing spells as there are melee charms, picking the best two or three and then facing diminishing returns as you scrape for anything else for your sorcerer to spend XP on wouldn't be a problem at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T13:47:38-07:00","id":1203976,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar497_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"497\" data-vbnamecard=\"497\">Xerxes</a>, Saying sorcery makes you buy just one charm is incorrect, you pay 3 points into occult just like you do MA, the cost for charm/compared to merit is relatively equal. Edit: another way to look at it is the charm is expressing the cost to gain sorcery in the mechanical sense, the initiation is the narrative (how) that it represents.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, you discounting how sorcerous initiations change the character in fundamental ways. A sorcerer initiated through Mara is by definition going to look at the world a hell of a lot differently than a person initiated through say a pact with an ifrit lord by virtue of the how (narratively) one needs to craft their initiation into their backstory.<br /> <br /> Further note: a SP stylist has around 10 total charms they can invest in, smaller in total than the amount of spells (and definitely from a utility aspect) and charms available to a solar sorcerer. Their MA charms at incompatible by design with both other MAs, and with all other ability charms. Are you telling me a sorcerer who invests in the 6 occult charms (six eternaties, ancient tounge, occulus, and all three circles) plus any additional spells, merits, and rituals, is less invested than a SP stylist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","user":"Saipjas","date":". 04-06-2018, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T15:38:41-07:00","id":1204014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203965#post1203965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">having some suggestions of what options sorcery opens up in terms of spending points on it the section that talks about spending points would have helped.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair cop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T18:34:29-07:00","id":1204058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1203976#post1203976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a