rum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204061#post1204061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...no it doesn't. I'm mostly tapped out here, but...like...no. Melee charms don't apply to Martial Arts attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWellll... Single Point Shining Into the Void provides a unique workaround, on account of its function of giving you an extra attack. You can't combo Melee and Martial Arts Charms in the same attack, but you <i>can</i> apply Melee Charms to your regular attack, and Single Point Charms to the one provided by the Form Charm.<br /> <br /> Not that I think that was what Lion Hamster was referring to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T19:56:35-07:00","id":1204081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204077#post1204077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWellll... Single Point Shining Into the Void provides a unique workaround, on account of its function of giving you an extra attack. You can't combo Melee and Martial Arts Charms in the same attack, but you <i>can</i> apply Melee Charms to your regular attack, and Single Point Charms to the one provided by the Form Charm.<br /> <br /> Not that I think that was what Lion Hamster was referring to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Snide... but correct, don't actually have much experience with combat characters, just sorcerers and socials","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T21:04:30-07:00","id":1204094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204061#post1204061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...no it doesn't. I'm mostly tapped out here, but...like...no. Melee charms don't apply to Martial Arts attacks. Athletics charms, ironically, do. And if you want <i>uber death kill</i> atheletics is mandatory for those sweet sweet damage multipliers. Shining Point is doubly screwed because as far as I'm aware, it only combos with 1other martial arts at the moment (steel devil).</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn\u2019t even really combine well with steel devil, due to how it\u2019s design really wants you to stay sheathed in between blows. Alucard made a good pint on Black claw, but even then it\u2019s a hard sell imo. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23635_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23635\" data-vbnamecard=\"23635\">Lion Hamster</a> as you have stated you don\u2019t have much experience with combat based chars I can kinda see a little bit more where you are coming from. Based upon your previous commentary you equate a DnD wizard with a sorcerer and are looking for sorcery to be able to function in combat analogues to that correct?<br /> <br /> A couple of brief things on casting in 3rd ed (I also play a sorcerer btw)<br /> <br /> At essence 1 a solar can chuck 20 dice while generating 1 SM from ancient tounge, have 1 exploding 10 from six eternities, and theoretically can generate an additional 1-3 SM from their sorcerous initiation. The total successes needed to gen up Death of Obsidian Butterflies (or Brilliant raptor) is 15 SM, given the previous math it takes less than 2 full rounds on average to sling a high power attack spell.<br /> <br /> For non-combat spells generating SMs is not a significant inhibitor. And thus your efficiency as a caster is honestly irrelevant in most cases.<br /> <br /> So what are you needing heavy boosters for your spells? The most costly Combat spell (Incomparable Body Arsenal) lasts 5 hours, in the event you are caught by surprise and are trying to gen it up fast, your sorcerous mote gen will be even faster due to have a secondary initiation, more draw from Ancient Tounge, and atleast 3 exploding 10s on your 20 dice that you are chucking around (the amount of exploding 10a granted from Eternities). <br /> <br /> If you are worried about Sorcerous workings at the solar level (let\u2019s go with ambition 3, and say you are wanting full control in how it is done so finesse 5)<br /> <br /> You need 75 Successes at the end of terminus for it to work, taking off 5 from each roll for finesse. If all you have are 5 rolls you would need an average of (napkin math) 20 success and yes that\u2019s pretty hard to get.<br /> <br /> However with 6 additional means (extending the interval 2 steps, cooperative caster, complementary spell, exotic components, complementary abilities) I just need an average of 12 successes to make it, easily within the scope. Now, does this take a metric assload of set up time? Absolutely but for changing the very rules of creation it should.<br /> <br /> My point in this long diatribe is to show you that the level of mechanical investiture you are asking for is a nice to have because the system as designed doesn\u2019t infact need more depth of charms to be able to do its ultimate schtick.<br /> <br /> Now, can you bemoan the lack of additional spells? Absolutely, but those will be forthcoming. I would urge you to please re-examine the crux of sorcery to be through the initiation rituals rather than charm support, because the system has to make since for sorcerers of ALL walks of life (not just Solars).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","user":"Saipjas","date":". 04-07-2018, 12:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{