 a highly power attack spell.<br /> <br /> For non-combat spells generating SMs is not a significant inhibitor. And thus your efficiency as a caster is honestly irrelevant in most cases.<br /> <br /> So what are you needing heavy boosters for your spells? The most costly Combat spell (Incomparable Body Arsenal) lasts 5 hours, in the event you are caught by surprise and are trying to gen it up fast, your sorcerous more gen will be even faster due to have a secondary initiation, more draw from Ancient Tounge, and atleast 3 exploding 10s on your 20 dice that you are chucking around (the amount of exploding 10a granted from Eternities).<br /> <br /> If you are worried about Sorcerous workings at the solar level (let\u2019s go with ambition 3, and say you are wanting full control in how it is done so finesse 5)<br /> <br /> You need 75 Successes at the end of terminus for it to work, taking off 5 from each roll for finesse. If all you have are 5 rolls you would need an average of (napkin math) 20 success and yes that\u2019s pretty hard to get.<br /> <br /> However with 6 additional means (extending the interval 2 steps, cooperative caster, complementary spell, exotic components, complementary abilities) I just need an average of 12 successes to make it, easily within the scope. Now, does this take a metric assload of set up time? Absolutely but for changing the very rules of creation it should.<br /> <br /> My point in this long diatribe is to show you that the level of mechanical investiture you are asking for is a nice to have because the system as designed doesn\u2019t infact need more depth of charms to be able to do its ultimate schtick.<br /> <br /> Now, can you bemoan the lack of additional spells? Absolutely, but those will be forthcoming. I would urge you to please re-examine the crux of sorcery to be through the initiation rituals rather than charm support, because the system has to make since for sorcerers of ALL walks of life (not just Solars).</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't how powerful sorcery is, the problem is it's not a proper character element, whether it's op or basically useless having no real charms leaves sorcerers with nothing to actually do with their xp related to sorcery, if you make a sorcerer 9/10 times you'll end up having a massive pile of xp that you can only spend on becoming something else","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T21:20:36-07:00","id":1204096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204095#post1204095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem isn't how powerful sorcery is, the problem is it's not a proper character element, whether it's op or basically useless having no real charms leaves sorcerers with nothing to actually do with their xp related to sorcery, if you make a sorcerer 9/10 times you'll end up having a massive pile of xp that you can only spend on becoming something else</div> </div> </div> </div>So that is where sorcerous workings come in to play, or homebrewing/transplanting spells from the white treatise into this edition as a stop-gap until the sorcery book is released (probably close to the heat death of the universe. However, we are as I stated earlier not going to see eye to eye. Because I feel the system does a sufficient job portraying a sorcerer as an identity and you do not. I feel you are judging everything by what a player can purchase via XP. Where I look at it going, what possibilities do workings and spells afford me for shaping the narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T21:25:15-07:00","id":1204098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204096#post1204096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So that is where sorcerous workings come in to play, or homebrewing/transplanting spells from the white treatise into this edition as a stop-gap until the sorcery book is released (probably close to the heat death of the universe. However, we are as I stated earlier not going to see eye to eye. Because I feel the system does a sufficient job portraying a sorcerer as an identity and you do not. I feel you are judging everything by what a player can purchase via XP. Where I look at it going, what possibilities do workings and spells afford me for shaping the narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember how people hated it when crafters were downtime wizards, this is very much the same problem workings will spend less xp over a longer time period than training skills and such","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T21:33:02-07:00","id":1204099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204098#post1204098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember how people hated it when crafters were downtime wizards, this is very much the same problem workings will spend less xp over a longer time period than training skills and such</div> </div> </div> </div>I get where you are coming from, but as I said way back when I feel you are trying to fit a square peg in a round hole precisely because of this viewpoint. Every game I have played in Exalted features high impact sessions, with weeks-months of downtime interspersed. So no I don\u2019t see that as a problem as it gives me things to narratively do during stretches of downtime. My circle has three sorcerers in it (our eclipse, me the twilight, and our dawn). Each has sorcery and not one has had the issues you are discussing, but that is because our circle does not view the system the way you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T21:45:13-07:00","id":1204101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204095#post1204095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem isn't how powerful sorcery is, the problem is it's not a proper character element, whether it's op or basically useless having no real charms leaves sorcerers with nothing to actually do with their xp related to sorcery, if you make a sorcerer 9/10 times you'll end up having a massive pile of xp that you can only spend on becoming something else</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm in a sort of quantum state of agreeing with you and disagreeing with you. One one hand, yeah, Sorcery isn't a charm tree and, unlike Martial Arts, it doesn't really benefit from the charms of other trees (as MA does with Dodge, Resistance, and Athletics).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Sorcery is clearly designed <i>not</i> to work like just another charm tree. It's not suppose to be something you mainline, moving through all the spells to become the Ultimate Mage\u2122, it's designed to be like an Expansion Pack onto stuff you can do. It's wholly separate from the other systems <i>on purpose</i>, because the effects of Sorcery are incredible, external, and alien to the rest of the system. In that sense I think it's a big success narratively and mechanically.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T21:58:43-07:00","id":1204103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204101#post1204101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in a sort of quantum state of agreeing with you and disagreeing with you. One one hand, yeah, Sorcery isn't a charm tree and, unlike Martial Arts, it doesn't really benefit from the charms of other trees (as MA does with Dodge, Resistance, and Athletics).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Sorcery is clearly designed <i>not</i> to work like just another charm tree. It's not suppose to be something you mainline, moving through all the spells to become the Ultimate Mage\u2122, it's designed to be like an Expansion Pack onto stuff you can do. It's wholly separate from the other systems <i>on purpose</i>, because the effects of Sorcery are incredible, external, and alien to the rest of the system. In that sense I think it's a big success narratively and mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue is there is no &quot;Ultimate mage&quot; in a spell battle someone who put 10xp into getting the charm doesn't get much more out of it then the one who focused on it to the exclusion of all else","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T22:29:54-07:00","id":1204110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204103#post1204103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issue is there is no &quot;Ultimate mage&quot; in a spell battle someone who put 10xp into getting the charm doesn't get much more out of it then the one who focused on it to the exclusion of all else</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for starters you get a bonus on counterspelling a spell you know/recognize. As to your second point, investiture in Sorcery opens up new avenues of expression, it doesn't add damage dice or distance modifiers like Melee and Athletics do. The Dawn who picks up ISoB gets a defense perk. The Twilight who did that, Demon of the First Circle, Summon Elemental, and Stormwind Rider can enter the fray commanding two separate battlegroups, <i>while</i> <i>flying</i>.<br /> <br /> Sorcery just isn't the Dice Modifier Charm tree you want it to be. It's a series of unique, non-overlapping abilities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T23:16:36-07:00","id":1204114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204103#post1204103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue is there is no &quot;Ultimate mage&quot; in a spell battle someone who put 10xp into getting the charm doesn't get much more out of it then the one who focused on it to the exclusion of all else</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would a character who's only invested 10 XP into sorcery get <i>more</i> out of it?<br /> <br /> Also, assuming you meant it the other way 'round, you're just plain wrong here. There's a world of difference between a guy with Att 1, Occult 3, [doing sorcery X] at you; and a guy with Att 5, Occult 5, a specialty in sorcery, picked the spell as his control spell, and has one or more initiation rituals or Merits that affect the spell, [doing sorcery X] at you.<br /> <br /> I sure know whose Death of Obsidian Butterflies I'd rather have to defend myself against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T23:31:16-07:00","id":1204116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204114#post1204114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a character who's only invested 10 XP into sorcery get <i>more</i> out of it?<br /> <br /> Also, assuming you meant it the other way 'round, you're just plain wrong here. There's a world of difference between a guy with Att 1, Occult 3, [doing sorcery X] at you; and a guy with Att 5, Occult 5, a specialty in sorcery, picked the spell as his control spell, and has one or more initiation rituals or Merits that affect the spell, [doing sorcery X] at you.<br /> <br /> I sure know whose Death of Obsidian Butterflies I'd rather have to defend myself against.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a wonderful point if any of that was correct but investing in sorcery makes it less likely that a given spell is your control, vastly less likely that your attribute will be at 5 and everyone gets an initiation ritual, you clearly don't know the basics of this system.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T23:44:21-07:00","id":1204117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204116#post1204116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be a wonderful point if any of that was correct but investing in sorcery makes it less likely that a given spell is your control, vastly less likely that your attribute will be at 5 and everyone gets an initiation ritual, you clearly don't know the basics of this system.</div> </div> </div> </div>...blinkingguy.gif look <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23635_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23635\" data-vbnamecard=\"23635\">Lion Hamster</a> people have tried to be respectful here, but let\u2019s set the record straight. Alucard is one of the more knowledgeable posters on the freaking board dude, I may have disagreed with him several times in the past, but he always has struck me as knowledgeable not just about the actual mechanics but also how the Devs have sought to shape the game.<br /> <br /> And I for the life of me an flabbergasted as to why in the Sam hell you\u2019d think a sorcerer would NOT invest Att 5/Abi 5 if they were wanting to excel not just in sorcery but in all aspects of the occult? I just really don\u2019t get your point here, other than you seem to be very frustrated that others don\u2019t see things the way you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T23:55:27-07:00","id":1204119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204117#post1204117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...blinkingguy.gif look <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23635_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23635\" data-vbnamecard=\"23635\">Lion Hamster</a> people have tried to be respectful here, but let\u2019s set the record straight. Alucard is one of the more knowledgeable posters on the freaking board dude, I may have disagreed with him several times in the past, but he always has struck me as knowledgeable not just about the actual mechanics but also how the Devs have sought to shape the game.<br /> <br /> And I for the life of me an flabbergasted as to why in the Sam hell you\u2019d think a sorcerer would NOT invest Att 5/Abi 5 if they were wanting to excel not just in sorcery but in all aspects of the occult? I just really don\u2019t get your point here, other than you seem to be very frustrated that others don\u2019t see things the way you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cause you can't invest in att 5 if you're going ham into sorcery cause there is no att for sorcery, each spell requires a different attribute and some don't even use occult","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T00:06:06-07:00","id":1204121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204119#post1204119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cause you can't invest in att 5 if you're going ham into sorcery cause there is no att for sorcery, each spell requires a different attribute and some don't even use occult</div> </div> </div> </div>Shape action is always Int+occult. Besides I wouldn't be too worried about the spread of xp around to cover different abilities and attributes, for one doing a quick scan over most of the spells in the core the only times the caster needs to make a roll Int or occult is used, meaning one is usually safe with an investment in both of those. Course since you were earlier arguing that sorcery was terrible because, &quot; if you make a sorcerer 9/10 times you'll end up having a massive pile of xp that you can only spend on becoming something else&quot; I would say covering those odd cases where 5 int or 5 occult isn't helping seems an excellent use for any extra xp one might have lying around that can't be used to buy non existent sorcery charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T00:10:53-07:00","id":1204124,"title":"","content":"At first, my take away was there wasn't a whole heck of a lot of support for Sorcerers in the Occult charm tree outside of the pre-req charms for initiation. At first take from memory that sounds about right to me. I can't say I'm all that happy about that outcome either as a lot of the spells aren't really my cup of tea at the moment. So, I too would appreciate some fresh ideas to make professional spellcasting appealing (as workings are hands down the only reason I'd bother with it atm).<br /> <br /> However, the longer I've tried to understand this thread, the more confused I've become as to what the actual agitation here is. I keep seeing non-specific assertions about likelihoods. Now as a former stats tutor, I'd love to see numbers to help illustrate where the perceived issue is, but really I'm just at a loss here.<br /> <br /> Normally I just prefer to lurk for information and occasionally ask questions, though this could possibly count as the latter... Really I'd like to think I have a well-formed impression of the regulars here, and I can tell they came with good intentions to examine what's going on. So please, assuming I'm not misinterpreting things from sheer fatigue, let's be a tad more civil in disagreeing in general here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T00:11:12-07:00","id":1204125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204119#post1204119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cause you can't invest in att 5 if you're going ham into sorcery cause there is no att for sorcery, each spell requires a different attribute and some don't even use occult</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally all shape sorcery actions are Int+Occult, you ability to cast requires that first and foremost. Corrupted Words, All summons, magma kraken, cantata of empty voices, and Death Ray use this as their primary stat. The non-rituals that don\u2019t that are not augmentation spells (such as WDC), are either transportation, non-stat spells (such as both mists and veil), or are the two attack spells DoOB and Raptor.<br /> <br /> Of these 2 DoOB is undodgeable, and rolling Occult+perception (a stat is likely to be atleast at 2-3 even if Int is 5), Raptor also has perception as it\u2019s other component. Both of which require 15 Sm to cast, meaning you want Int 5 so you can chuck those babies close to every round, sacrificing 1-2 die on the attack roll to get them off faster is in most cases a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T00:11:15-07:00","id":1204126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204121#post1204121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shape action is always Int+occult. Besides I wouldn't be too worried about the spread of xp around to cover different abilities and attributes, for one doing a quick scan over most of the spells in the core the only times the caster needs to make a roll Int or occult is used, meaning one is usually safe with an investment in both of those. Course since you were earlier arguing that sorcery was terrible because, &quot; if you make a sorcerer 9/10 times you'll end up having a massive pile of xp that you can only spend on becoming something else&quot; I would say covering those odd cases where 5 int or 5 occult isn't helping seems an excellent use for any extra xp one might have lying around that can't be used to buy non existent sorcery charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, just no<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T00:12:19-07:00","id":1204127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204126#post1204126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, just no</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, sparky it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T00:19:37-07:00","id":1204128,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13326_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13326\" data-vbnamecard=\"13326\">Aredin</a> the conflict is essentially a worldview conflict. For instance I contend there is a sufficient amount of material that being a sorcerer feels different (narratively) than a non-sorcerer. The other school of thought wishes there was more mechanical investiture (ie spending XP) to show this through the purchase of sorcery boosting charms. What I was attempting to show up thread was that you really didn\u2019t need much more than are already available to get the most out of sorcery. Overlords point as well is that sorcery should not be viewed as a charm tree but rather it\u2019s own thing that gives the character new avenues to approach situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T00:48:53-07:00","id":1204135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204128#post1204128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13326_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13326\" data-vbnamecard=\"13326\">Aredin</a> the conflict is essentially a worldview conflict. For instance I contend there is a sufficient amount of material that being a sorcerer feels different (narratively) than a non-sorcerer. The other school of thought wishes there was more mechanical investiture (ie spending XP) to show this through the purchase of sorcery boosting charms. What I was attempting to show up thread was that you really didn\u2019t need much more than are already available to get the most out of sorcery. Overlords point as well is that sorcery should not be viewed as a charm tree but rather it\u2019s own thing that gives the character new avenues to approach situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>For awhile it seemed like people talking past each other, but your assessment seems more accurate than mine.<br /> <br /> While I'm here though I may as well say the only thing I'd really need to get the most out of sorcery is access to workings and maybe Whirlwind Rider, as everything else for one reason or another, has a thematic clash with my personal taste in building characters, or a feeling of incompleteness (such as the case with Summon Elemental). Were I to seek (in munchkin fashion) an outlet for spending SXP on magic/powers, it'd easily rank below Martial Arts and Evocations for me because of my desired style in characters. So I can kind of see the base frustration (though the specific arguments aren't where my issues lie).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin","name":"Aredin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13326_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T00:59:48-07:00","id":1204136,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13326_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13326\" data-vbnamecard=\"13326\">Aredin</a>, I can get the frustration, I just happen to feel that it is a matter of expectations not jiving with the design intent of sorcery. Sorcery can have room for investiture, but as of now requires either extensive porting of spells from the white treatise, homebrew or porting of various elementals/demons, or downtime in the form of sorcerous workings (which also require homebrew). The whole thrust of what I have been trying to say though is that being a sorcerer is as much an identity as being a solar is, unique and different. Sorcery, due to its nature as overlord observed existing outside of each type of exalt, is its own separate system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T01:03:07-07:00","id":1204137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204136#post1204136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13326-aredin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13326_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13326\" data-vbnamecard=\"13326\">Aredin</a>, I can get the frustration, I just happen to feel that it is a matter of expectations not jiving with the design intent of sorcery. Sorcery can have room for investiture, but as of now requires either extensive porting of spells from the white treatise, homebrew or porting of various elementals/demons, or downtime in the form of sorcerous workings (which also require homebrew). The whole thrust of what I have been trying to say though is that being a sorcerer is as much an identity as being a solar is, unique and different. Sorcery, due to its nature as overlord observed existing outside of each type of exalt, is its own separate system.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's just not how solar charms work, solars don't have their charms predecided like siddies, it's just a manIfestation of them being <i>reeeeeeally</i> good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T01:11:08-07:00","id":1204138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204137#post1204137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's just not how solar charms work, solars don't have their charms predecided like siddies, it's just a manIfestation of them being <i>reeeeeeally</i> good</div> </div> </div> </div>And the solar charms that boost sorcery reflect that, (ancient tounge, six eternities). But occult is more than just sorcery, Occult is about all the the weirdness of Creation. It\u2019s the ability to at a glance know exactly how a spell, working, or artifact can operate. Its the ability to destroy spirits and take their powers for your own, it\u2019s the ability to bind/repel spirits or give birth to spirits whole cloth. It\u2019s the power to gain abilities of spirits as your own, and finally it\u2019s the ability to tap into ancient knowledge to empower your sorcery through ancient tounges.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is just one aspect of occult, and since sorcery is its own system that has to operate with ALL, it gets imo a sufficient amount of place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T03:11:12-07:00","id":1204150,"title":"","content":"As a personal note, I'd love the devs to pieces if a hypothetical Sorcery book made it even remotely viable to focus on spells to the exclusion of charms. The 'Brigid build' as it were. I don't need charms or even Evocations that interract with sorcery: having enough spells to use a wide variety like that is quite enough for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T05:04:21-07:00","id":1204156,"title":"","content":"Only really read the first few pages, so may be coming late to this conversation, but my thinking at the moment is as follows: There's a bit of a disconnect here between this thread, where there seems to be a desire for more hierarchical, deep structure within spells (cf Aquillion?), and the immediate reception of sorcery in 3e.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of biased against the idea of adding more structure and pre-requisites and hierarchy to another subsystem, and salami slicing the power in spells across subtrees, and adding more weight, just for the purposes of making it soak up as much xp sink as other functions and then an effect from this on the perception of a character as a sorcerer. <br /> <br /> (To me this all is seeming to give me slight eerie flashbacks similar to some 2e thinking where sorcery was mentally reduced in the forum conversation to something that *had* to be a slightly problematic Jack-of-All-Trades, Master-of-None capability in order to balance with Charms, so neither was a &quot;superior&quot; or &quot;inferior&quot; option. Which was all absolutely a wrongheaded way of thinking about what the differences between sorcery and Charms are and should be!)<br /> <br /> I'd be more inclined to question why players like Wizard's mentioned on pag 1 seem to have gone elaborately all in for sorcery when others do not, and to me that seems to be maybe more about that player embracing the sorcerous aesthetic and differences in her goals for that character, than that player pursuing a path which is mechanically suboptimal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T05:30:52-07:00","id":1204161,"title":"","content":"So I have run and played in two separate year long games since 3e came out. In both, we had characters for whom being a sorcerer was a defining character trait. In both, we ended up updating some spells from 2e Black and White Treatise for more spell options, which was pretty easy in most cases.<br /> <br /> One of our sorcerers was an Occult Supernal Twilight whose backstory was that he'd been offered as a human sacrifice to an Ifrit Lord as a baby, and had been raised by a confused-by-children but generally genial Big Fire Dad. He took lots of fire spells and his Father's burning name on his lips was a mighty weapon. He summoned elementals constantly and kept them in his Anima and sometimes released them into the wild with orders like &quot;go protect the city's children&quot; or &quot;go teach people to have more fun!&quot; His mastery of Occult let him steal tricks and powers from the spiits he treated with, and enabled his eventual ability to spiritually tear apart and devour an evil ghost, which caused him to get infected with Whispers and become a lot less happy-go-lucky. He cheered up a bit after he forged a sweet Phoenix familiar from the fires of his own soul using Occult charms, and they came in very handy for figuring out the schemes of the enemy sorcerers of Ysyr. In combat he was brutally effective and fond of finishing fights with Flight of the Brilliant Raptor. Sacrificed his life to save Creation from the Eyeless Face. Sorcery seemed fine as a central conceit for him.<br /> <br /> Second one was Night Caste socialite, sneak, and general Bad Decision Dinosaur. He picked up sorcery partway through the game, and it was a character defining and character altering thing. We played out his meeting with Mara and learning from her, knowing she was dangerous and not trusting her but trying to get as much knowledge and power as he could without owing her too much. The two of them had an elaborate &quot;who owes who favors&quot; thing going on, and he took less fight and more utilitarian spells mostly involving bird themes and shadow themes. He only had a small handful of spells, but Flight of Separation updated from 2e completely changed his play experience and Mara kept offering to teach him more spells suited to his current problems to get him into her debt. He wasn't super fighty...until he summoned Gervesin. He traumatized a demon Lord by going into Limit Break while possessed and taking total control and leaving a trail of green fire and senseless destruction far beyond what Gervesin wanted, and got dragged into Hellish politics and intrigue because now multiple second circle demons were trying to pull him in different directions. Sorcery was, for him, a way to explore the temptations of playing with Dark Powers. He spent a lot of time worried about getting eaten and did multiple workings to make himself incredibly poisonous to demons and other creatures of darkness.<br /> <br /> Number 3 was a Twilight with a &quot;brightly colored and poisonous&quot; theme who wrote fanfic and tried to make it a reality. He was an Alchemist, and dipped into Craft and Medicine for brewing potions and salves, and he did sorcery by spiritually perfecting himself through ascetiscism and a vegetarian diet. He did a ton of workings from the very beginning. He gave himself poisonous blood, he enchanted Grandmother Bright's neighborhood in Chiarascuro with Disneyesque living brooms that cleaned up at night, he gave the Night Caste gills so she could breathe underwater and he bred a new strain of incredibly Hardy magic kudzu that could survive almost any climate and was highly edible in an effort to solve world hunger. He turned his snake familiar into a two hundred foot dragon with poisonous needles for scales who could devour ingredients to excrete potions or alchemical compounds through her needles like a living alchemical lab. By Solar Circle, plants and flowers sprung up in his sacred footsteps and withered and died at his merest displeasure. His biggest problem was not that charms didn't provide him an increasing amount of power, it was that he had a limited array of abilities to solve a given problem that wouldn't also wipe out whatever city he was in. He built his fanfic world in the Wild with lore charms and raw will power, and then did a Working to keep his city inside a gem he wore around his neck. He once freed an entire army of demons in a fit of ideological pique about the unethical nature of slavery, and he had to be talked out of forcing world Peace by carving a Linguistics Charm enhanced poem into the surface of the Moon with Death Ray.<br /> <br /> ... What I am getting at here is that sorcery works just fine for enabling play of a bunch different playstyles and thematic kinds of sorcerers. Breadth matters more than power: a melee guy who gets a new charm gets the power to do his thing (murder) better, but no new options. A sorcerer who gets a new spell gets a new OPTION: she can fly hundreds of miles in a day now, or call up a city destroying tsunami, or summon up a pavilion to feed and shelter the injured when her city suffers an earthquake. Workings multiply her options by infinity. Sure, a Supernal Brawl guy can smash her face in...but he probably won't wreck up her enchanted sewer system because nobody wants the smell from before she installed it back!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T08:43:45-07:00","id":1204188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204161#post120