card","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:10:56-07:00","id":1204579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204563#post1204563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One time, he went into the Silver Forest to try and find an alternate universe version of himself that was less of a human disaster to replace himself with for the good of humanity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOhhh my God that's amazing. <br /> <br /> \u200bHas there ever been a Marvel or DC character who tried something like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T05:47:09-07:00","id":1205151,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. I don't know about setting out to do it <i>intentionally</i>, but something like that happened to the supporting character Cal in Mike Carey's <i>Lucifer</i> series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T01:34:03-07:00","id":1208763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1204161#post1204161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..., and he had to be talked out of forcing world Peace by carving a Linguistics Charm enhanced poem into the surface of the Moon with Death Ray.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did your player by any chance read the J.M.Troska books?<br /> <br /> The sorcery sub-system (Sorcery) in Ex3 does by design have a small number of charms that interact with it. Because the Sorcery is by itself very flexible and it would be hard to balance more exotic charms against that flexibility. There are similarities between how you leverage power from Craft and Sorcery. The main power and of crafting comes from the evocations that you can unlock on your artifacts. We got sample evocations and artifacts, but the expectation is that people will heavily homebrew and customize. Similarly, in Sorcery, we got few sample initiations and spells, but the expectation is also that people will heavily customize.<br /> <br /> Now how is a character heavily invested in sorcery (a Sorcerer) different from a mere dabbler that got just the charms and a few spells?<br /> <br /> <b>Opening more &quot;rituals&quot; for your initiation</b>: These should mostly provide you with utility <i>powers</i> (flaming breath, poisonous touch, hearing lies, etc.) or enhance your ability to generate and accumulate motes (utility in combat is self-explanatory). Remember that you can also have more than one initiation into the same circle to have more flexibility.<br /> <br /> <b>Learning new spells</b>: Different spells mostly provide utility, the Ex3 has quite a few printed, you can adopt more from the previous editions or just create your own.<br /> <br /> <b>Working</b>: Now this is the area where the person that does heavily invest into sorcery does most of the investing and it should show. First, getting back XP for workings that are no longer relevant is similar to the idea that you should get reimbursed for a charm/artifact/etc. that you somehow lost access to. But the main progress should come from the workings you keep.<br /> <br /> One design space of workings, are the workings that will increase your means, thus making it easier for you to make harder workings in the future. The other design space is all about utility.<br /> <br /> And the utility of the Sorcery system is strong. Do you invest heavily in the Athletic to gain the ability to fly or do you just learn one spell, make a working on your shoes or gain initiation from an Air spirit?<br /> <br /> Hell if you want something that feels more like &quot;casting&quot; spells: Pick a short stick (a wand), make a Solar Finesse 5 working on it and now when you point the wand and say the keyword &quot;Avada Kedavra&quot;, your victim is most likely dead, struck by X un-soakable aggravated damage. And you can &quot;learn&quot; more spells for your wand.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And all but the Charms could be paid for by Solar XP so you should have plenty of opportunities to invest in Charms in other trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","user":"Korusef","date":". 04-19-2018, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T09:01:48-07:00","id":1208903,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\">Lion Hamster, I'm becoming vexed by your attitude. Where do you get off saying that someone whose whole character concept isn't dedicated to sorcery isn't a \u201creal sorcerer\u201d even if its a profound and important part of their life and identity? Someone's example a few pages ago was a smith whose sorcerous initiation was part of <i>their relationship to their god</i> and you're just like \u201cthey're a crafter not a sorcerer\u201d because apparently if you're a sorcerer it has to be the only thing you are. You're taking a dump on a lot of people's character concepts when you say that, do you realise that? I never thought I'd see someone gatekeeping the idea of roleplaying a sorcerer. <br /> <br /> What does a &quot;real sorcerer&quot; even look like to you? The fact that you have to spend xp elsewhere shouldn't dilute your status as a sorcerer and indeed <i>should</i> be necessary to realise most character concepts related to sorcery. The most learned scholar of the arcane who devotes himself to the mysteries of the cosmos is probably going to be a Lore supernal rather than Occult, and that's the most archetypal and &quot;pure&quot; sorcerer concept there is. The hero who tricked the secret of magic out of the fae and brought its gifts back to his people, transforming their society with his works, is supernal Larceny or Socialise, and is as much about Wits and Manipulation as Intelligence. The sorceress who composed a sonata that made the heavens weep and the desert bloom into fertile land is just as much about Performance as sorcery (and has high Charisma to match), but she's still very much a sorceress. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">This is Exalted, the fact that characters aren't nailed down into specific narrow classes and you can blend the themes of multiple power-sets to achieve your character concept is a </span><i>strength of the system</i><span style=\"color:#000000\">. Maybe if your idea of \u201cbeing a real sorcerer\u201d wasn't so prescriptive you would actually see the point of spells like Corrupted Words. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">I'll agree that Solar workings are harder for a maxed-out sorcerer than legendary projects are for a maxed-out crafter, but that has more to do with the Craft tree being ludicrously overbuilt than any problem with sorcery. They're both meant to be epically difficult. </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">At the end of the day, if you really want the &quot;ten different ways to reroll dice&quot; approach from Craft applied to sorcerous workings, and your ST is cool with it, those are some of the easiest Charms to re-skin for another Ability. Under no circumstances would I allow them to apply to Shape Sorcery actions though - that level of dice-trickery does not belong in combat. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T00:02:33-07:00","id":1209131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1208903#post1208903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Lion Hamster, I'm becoming vexed by your attitude. Where do you get off saying that someone whose whole character concept isn't dedicated to sorcery isn't a \u201creal sorcerer\u201d even if its a profound and important part of their life and identity? Someone's example a few pages ago was a smith whose sorcerous initiation was part of <i>their relationship to their god</i> and you're just like \u201cthey're a crafter not a sorcerer\u201d because apparently if you're a sorcerer it has to be the only thing you are. You're taking a dump on a lot of people's character concepts when you say that, do you realise that? I never thought I'd see someone gatekeeping the idea of roleplaying a sorcerer.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>&gt;What's the difference between a sorcerer and a Sorcerer<br /> &gt;Why doesn't my Swordsman diplomat scholar brawler martial artist painter who also learnt stormwind rider at essence 4 count as a sorcerer<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1208903#post1208903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">What does a &quot;real sorcerer&quot; even look like to you? The fact that you have to spend xp elsewhere shouldn't dilute your status as a sorcerer and indeed <i>should</i> be necessary to realise most character concepts related to sorcery. The most learned scholar of the arcane who devotes himself to the mysteries of the cosmos is probably going to be a Lore supernal rather than Occult, and that's the most archetypal and &quot;pure&quot; sorcerer concept there is. The hero who tricked the secret of magic out of the fae and brought its gifts back to his people, transforming their society with his works, is supernal Larceny or Socialise, and is as much about Wits and Manipulation as Intelligence. The sorceress who composed a sonata that made the heavens weep and the desert bloom into fertile land is just as much about Performance as sorcery (and has high Charisma to match), but she's still very much a sorceress. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>&gt;The most pure sorcery concept isn't focused on sorcery<br /> Yes, that's the problem","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23635,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","user":"Lion Hamster","date":". 04-20-2018, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T14:23:00-07:00","id":1209398,"title":"","content":"Lion Hamster, I'm not sure I understand what the root of the problem is here. Are there just not enough spells (and/or Occult Charms that benefit sorcery) for your taste?<br /> <br /> Do you want it to be feasible for a sorcerer to buy only (or primarily) spells, and no (or few) non-sorcery Charms, and still be an effective character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T14:27:32-07:00","id":1209399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209398#post1209398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lion Hamster, I'm not sure I understand what the root of the problem is here. Are there just not enough spells (and/or Occult Charms that benefit sorcery) for your taste?<br /> <br /> Do you want it to be feasible for a sorcerer to buy only (or primarily) spells, and no (or few) non-sorcery Charms, and still be an effective character?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've gathered Hamster's complaint is that solar sorcerers are supposed to be the best, and this is depicted by getting access to powers everyone else needs workings to accomplish and to extend their reach to attempt as opposed to having the occult tree dedicated entirely to just allowing solars to spam spells and be dnd munchkin wizards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T14:47:48-07:00","id":1209409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209399#post1209399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've gathered Hamster's complaint is that solar sorcerers are supposed to be the best, and this is depicted by getting access to powers everyone else needs workings to accomplish and to extend their reach to attempt as opposed to having the occult tree dedicated entirely to just allowing solars to spam spells and be dnd munchkin wizards.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I'd say this doesn't appear to be 100% inaccurate, it does seem to be moderately misrepresentative. Not to mention dismissive.<br /> <br /> It seems more to focus on the idea that a Solar sorceror who dedicates himself entirely to Sorcery isn't that much different from anyone else who dedicates themselves entirely to Sorcery except in dice pools and access to the highest tier of spells, which Hamster seems to think is not enough to make a Solar Sorceror concept cool to him.<br /> <br /> There are a few valid criticisms in his statements, but I admit I don't see it that way.<br /> <br /> However, for full disclosure, I have yet to be allowed to be a player and mess with sorcery in any extensive sort of way. So I may not have the perspective to argue the point that clearly. But from my view, Solar Sorcery is still awesome and great, and I don't think that Sorcery being blended with other things sometimes makes Sorcery any less a focus for the character, any more than Melee being mixed with Dodge and Resistance makes the swordsman less of a swordsman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T15:03:47-07:00","id":1209416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krata Lightblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209409#post1209409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While I'd say this doesn't appear to be 100% inaccurate, it does seem to be moderately misrepresentative. Not to mention dismissive.<br /> <br /> It seems more to focus on the idea that a Solar sorceror who dedicates himself entirely to Sorcery isn't that much different from anyone else who dedicates themselves entirely to Sorcery except in dice pools and access to the highest tier of spells, which Hamster seems to think is not enough to make a Solar Sorceror concept cool to him.<br /> <br /> There are a few valid criticisms in his statements, but I admit I don't see it that way.<br /> <br /> However, for full disclosure, I have yet to be allowed to be a player and mess with sorcery in any extensive sort of way. So I may not have the perspective to argue the point that clearly. But from my view, Solar Sorcery is still awesome and great, and I don't think that Sorcery being blended with other things sometimes makes Sorcery any less a focus for the character, any more than Melee being mixed with Dodge and Resistance makes the swordsman less of a swordsman.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd argue not really that misreprestative as he's argued those points at various intervals. He's argued workings are too hard to accomplish, that no charms means you just end up with piles of useless xp because a sorcerer has nothing to spend it on, that the occult tree does nothing to make one a better sorcerer, that there are no skills or attributes to pick to make one a better sorcerer. The only point he's gotten that I could agree with was that deciding to be a sorcerer doesn't inherently make it the focus of my character, which I see as more of a feature than a bug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T15:57:25-07:00","id":1209431,"title":"","content":"The actual points he made are moderately more complex than &quot;He isn't a D&amp;D blaster wizard&quot; is all I was getting at. I don't really agree with all of his criticism either, but reductive statements tend to end up being countered by other reductive statements and eventually you end up with politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T15:59:45-07:00","id":1209434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krata Lightblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209409#post1209409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that Sorcery being blended with other things sometimes makes Sorcery any less a focus for the character, any more than Melee being mixed with Dodge and Resistance makes the swordsman less of a swordsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing wrong with mixing sorcery with other archetypes but there's a reason it's always a diplomat sorcerer or a warrior sorcerer or a craftsman sorcerer not a sorcerer diplomat or a sorcerer warrior or a sorcerer craftsman","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:01:08-07:00","id":1209435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209416#post1209416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue not really that misreprestative as he's argued those points at various intervals. He's argued workings are too hard to accomplish, that no charms means you just end up with piles of useless xp because a sorcerer has nothing to spend it on, that the occult tree does nothing to make one a better sorcerer, that there are no skills or attributes to pick to make one a better sorcerer. The only point he's gotten that I could agree with was that deciding to be a sorcerer doesn't inherently make it the focus of my character, which I see as more of a feature than a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fantastic combination of things that are non-sequitur and things that are just correct<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:09:51-07:00","id":1209443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209434#post1209434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's nothing wrong with mixing sorcery with other archetypes but there's a reason it's always a diplomat sorcerer or a warrior sorcerer or a craftsman sorcerer not a sorcerer diplomat or a sorcerer warrior or a sorcerer craftsman</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not 100% sure I'd agree with that statement, though I can see from your posts where you'd come up with that assertion. I think it's more a mindset thing than a game problem, personally, as if it were a universal game issue you wouldn't have so many counterpoints to your assertion.<br /> <br /> That said, I've always seen Sorcery in Exalted as an... envelope, of sorts. It sits over and covers everything else you are, by virtue of what it is. You're now a Sorceror. You deal with strange powers, weird creatures, and terrifying magic. If Sorcery is any significant part of your concept, the world treats you like a Not Normal Person. Now, your assertion is largely that the mechanics don't back this up, as I understand it. That the &quot;optimal&quot; path for a Sorceror is to use Sorcery as a supplement. I'd argue that Sorcery is a path that requires creativity, a willingness to do things in nonstandard ways, and a change in mindset to really come off as truly the path of the Sorceror.<br /> <br /> Will you be more mechanically effective than the guy who buys three spells and spends the rest of his XP on something else? Maybe, maybe not, depends on how you use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T16:17:08-07:00","id":1209447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209131#post1209131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;What's the difference between a sorcerer and a Sorcerer<br /> &gt;Why doesn't my Swordsman diplomat scholar brawler martial artist painter who also learnt stormwind rider at essence 4 count as a sorcerer</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, the person you just described sounds like a dabbler. But that wasn't really what I was talking about. You must know that too, you're just being intellectually dishonest to avoid engaging with my point, which leads me to believe you know you're wrong, which leads me to believe that you're just trolling at this point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209131#post1209131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;The most pure sorcery concept isn't focused on sorcery<br /> Yes, that's the problem</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the purest sorcery concept isn't focused on <i>Occult</i>. Why should it be? Archetypal wizards are typically scholars, Lore is the &quot;being a scholar&quot; Ability. If your sorcerer is more of a shaman by background, you pick Occult. If your initiation focuses on magical calligraphy, maybe go for Linguistics. No problem. The difference between a master calligrapher who has mastered sorcery and one who hasn't will be immediately obvious because the sorcerer's skin will be thick with tattoos of enchanted poems that grant him power, and when he casts a spell or addresses a crowd his utterances appear before him in the air as burning words of power. But because he has a bunch of Linguistics and Presence Charms he's not a &quot;real sorcerer&quot; to you? <br /> <br /> No comment on the paragraph where I tried to help you solve your problem, even to tell me I was off the mark? It's almost like you don't want to be helped and are just trolling. <br /> <br /> If you really don't grok what the point of exalted sorcery is (and despite your demonstrated mechanical knowledge I'm not sure you do), maybe try something else instead, like Brawl. In fact, try to make a brawler who is just as much of a Brawler and you want sorcerers to be Sorcerers. Remember, you shouldn't need to invest in other Abilities to be good at your one thing, so don't bother with Athletics, Awareness, Dodge or Resistance. And the attack roll for Brawl is Dexterity+Brawl so it's perfectly reasonable to be the Best Brawler without decent Strength or Wits, no matter what anyone tells you. Let us know how it goes. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T17:35:46-07:00","id":1209459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209435#post1209435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A fantastic combination of things that are non-sequitur and things that are just correct<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Word of advice before you call something a non-sequitur make sure you know what that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T17:39:15-07:00","id":1209460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209447#post1209447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, the person you just described sounds like a dabbler. But that wasn't really what I was talking about. You must know that too, you're just being intellectually dishonest to avoid engaging with my point, which leads me to believe you know you're wrong, which leads me to believe that you're just trolling at this point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, the purest sorcery concept isn't focused on <i>Occult</i>. Why should it be? Archetypal wizards are typically scholars, Lore is the &quot;being a scholar&quot; Ability. If your sorcerer is more of a shaman by background, you pick Occult. If your initiation focuses on magical calligraphy, maybe go for Linguistics. No problem. The difference between a master calligrapher who has mastered sorcery and one who hasn't will be immediately obvious because the sorcerer's skin will be thick with tattoos of enchanted poems that grant him power, and when he casts a spell or addresses a crowd his utterances appear before him in the air as burning words of power. But because he has a bunch of Linguistics and Presence Charms he's not a &quot;real sorcerer&quot; to you?<br /> <br /> No comment on the paragraph where I tried to help you solve your problem, even to tell me I was off the mark? It's almost like you don't want to be helped and are just trolling.<br /> <br /> If you really don't grok what the point of exalted sorcery is (and despite your demonstrated mechanical knowledge I'm not sure you do), maybe try something else instead, like Brawl. In fact, try to make a brawler who is just as much of a Brawler and you want sorcerers to be Sorcerers. Remember, you shouldn't need to invest in other Abilities to be good at your one thing, so don't bother with Athletics, Awareness, Dodge or Resistance. And the attack roll for Brawl is Dexterity+Brawl so it's perfectly reasonable to be the Best Brawler without decent Strength or Wits, no matter what anyone tells you. Let us know how it goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence you see what we've been dealing with. This is not a debate so much as someone wanting to say something is broken and nonfunctional and refusing to countenance arguments, and in some cases, proof that its just things not matching with their opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T17:55:19-07:00","id":1209461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209460#post1209460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence you see what we've been dealing with. This is not a debate so much as someone wanting to say something is broken and nonfunctional and refusing to countenance arguments, and in some cases, proof that its just things not matching with their opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading through this thread the problem looks to be on both sides of people just talking past each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T21:35:04-07:00","id":1209507,"title":"","content":"Pretty much he just wants something like a Sorcery tree in Occult. I can see that.<br /> <br /> In my game we made an Occult charm at essence 2 that speeds up Terrestrial workings, then a repurchase at essence 4 that speeds up Celestial ones. I can totally see more charms that do stuff like that and the Devs have said that such charms are fine, they're just not in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T23:48:01-07:00","id":1209530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kunoichi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/28651-dreams?p=120950#post120950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my game we made an Occult charm at essence 2 that speeds up Terrestrial workings, then a repurchase at essence 4 that speeds up Celestial ones. I can totally see more charms that do stuff like that and the Devs have said that such charms are fine, they're just not in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cite, please? The last statement I saw from the Devs was that decreasing the intervals for sorcerous workings was <i>not</i> fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/754484-ex3-sorcery-negative-means?p=754770#post754770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, and for that exact reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T00:27:13-07:00","id":1209537,"title":"","content":"I can't sift through a multi-hundred page thread for something like this, but I recall them saying that making charms that interact with sorcery are okay.<br /> <br /> As for what the charm in question did, was it simply brought down the interval by one step from weeks to days. It was based on being something similar to Thousand-Forge Hands since my Twilight player didn't want to wait forever to do all the stuff he wanted to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T00:40:40-07:00","id":1209539,"title":"","content":"Whoah that's powerful.<br /> <br /> But saying that, if you're doing the sort of game where you never get any downtime, I guess you kind of have to.<br /> <br /> In the game I used to run, the Solar sorcerer had something like 10 workings, many of them quite significant. Being able to do workings in days would be far too powerful.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, in the game I've been playing for years, we hardly ever have downtime more than 1-2 days, so only one (small) working has ever actually got done. <br /> <br /> A bit tricky for the writers to balance, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T00:54:37-07:00","id":1209544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209434#post1209434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's nothing wrong with mixing sorcery with other archetypes but there's a reason it's always a diplomat sorcerer or a warrior sorcerer or a craftsman sorcerer not a sorcerer diplomat or a sorcerer warrior or a sorcerer craftsman</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, this isn't true.<br /> For most sorcerers in the early-to-mid game, and some sorcerers in the late game, sorcery is their main thing. It's just so dramatic and obvious.<br /> <br /> For example, in one game I play we have a Sorcerer Queen. When you think of her, you absolutely think &quot;sorcery&quot;. She has a bunch of summoned demon advisors (Alveua, Florivet, Makarios, and that spite-dragon woman I think?), invulnerable bronze skin, rides a dragon she made with sorcery, and her most iconic combat power is Death Ray. She rules a magical kingdom of people she heavily modified with sorcery. Secondarily, she can parry blows well, ride really fast, stab people reasonably well (but not, for an Essence 5 Solar, particularly well), roll decent but not amazing social attacks, etc.<br /> <br /> In the game my friends play, the Twilight is a sorcerer/doctor. He does have a lot of medicine charms, but his primary thing is sorcery, and they live in a giant floating castle with its own Sun that he made.<br /> <br /> In the game I previously played, we had two sorcerers. The twilight sorcerer was a sorcerer... noble? Architect? I'm not sure because sorcery was the more obvious thing, to me at least.<br /> My own sorcerer was a sorcerer/shapeshifter. I'd say those two things were roughly even.<br /> <br /> Now, in the late game, I did find we suddenly had a rash of people with sorcery as a minor focus. But that's because in the late game, people have spent a ton of XP on their main thing are looking for extra bits. Of course, they're minor.<br /> For example, the Appearance-charm Lunar &gt; the Appearance-charm/kung-fu Lunar &gt; the Appearance-charm/kung-fu/territorial Lunar &gt; the Appearance-charm/kung-fu/territorial/sorcerer Lunar.<br /> And the Crafter &gt; Crafter/Doctor &gt; Crafter/Doctor/Thief &gt; Crafter/Doctor/Thief/Swordsman &gt; Crafter/Doctor/Thief/Swordsman/Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Essentially, every focus is something you can't focus 100% on, or you'd have a very boring character (and generally, mid-game, you'd run out of charms to get anyway, unless you're a Crafter). I mean, if your swordsman has 20 melee charms and nothing else... man, that's dull.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I do kind of agree with you that sorcery may not actually involve a lot of charm slots. My Sorcerer/Shapeshifter had a lot more knacks than spells (maybe 14 spells and 21 knacks? Something like that). And it would be nice to have more spells (and we'll get a few more on Wednesday!).<br /> <br /> But sorcery has greater thematic weight than other stuff, because it's so dramatic and flashy.<br /> Similarly, I think my friend's Twilight character Lao has more Medicine charms than XP put into spells/workings, but since sorcery is more dramatic than medicine charms, it forms a larger part of the character (I think, I haven't played the game. But everyone tells me he's a sorcerer, he does all these wacky workings, and also he can heal people which is why they keep him around despite all the dodgy evil magic he does).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-21-2018, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T01:24:12-07:00","id":1209551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209544#post1209544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and we'll get a few more on Wednesday!</div> </div> </div> </div>We will? Where?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T01:34:00-07:00","id":1209554,"title":"","content":"The DB kickstarter. If you've signed up for it, they send out chapters from the book (but just the plain text, no art, etc).<br /> <br /> They've now sent out all the fluff and DB charms, so this week should have Martial Arts, spells and evocations (and maybe a storytelling chapter).<br /> <br /> MA will be 8 styles, but I don't know how many spells there will be, except that it's &quot;some&quot;, and they're stuff relevant to Terrestrials.<br /> So I guess they'll all be Terrestrial Circle, and probably elemental in nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T03:32:05-07:00","id":1209567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209554#post1209554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The DB kickstarter. If you've signed up for it, they send out chapters from the book (but just the plain text, no art, etc).<br /> <br /> They've now sent out all the fluff and DB charms, so this week should have Martial Arts, spells and evocations (and maybe a storytelling chapter).</div> </div> </div> </div>MA, spells, evocations, and QC Dragon-Blooded. No storytelling chapter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T03:47:14-07:00","id":1209569,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. QCs are more useful to me and my group than a Storytelling Chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T13:57:20-07:00","id":1209771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209530#post1209530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cite, please? The last statement I saw from the Devs was that decreasing the intervals for sorcerous workings was <i>not</i> fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you look at that thread, the question wasn't &quot;can you decrease the interval at all?&quot; but rather &quot;can you decrease the interval in exchange for having 'negative Means' [i.e. reducing the terminus of the project]?&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, that doesn't necessarily mean decreasing the interval in general <i>is</i> fine either. I would be surprised, though, if it wasn't possible under any circumstances; I can't think how reducing the amount of downtime you need could be a serious game balance problem. (And if it is, I'm not sure why it would be okay for craftsmen and not sorcerers. Thousand-Forge Hands is a <i>massive</i> time reducer.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T14:38:16-07:00","id":1209777,"title":"","content":"Craft is an odd one, because it doesn't require much downtime, but it does require you to get all those Craft points. Those are the real limiter (until you Charm your way past it, at which point it's the materials needed that are the limiter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T17:40:17-07:00","id":1209834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209777#post1209777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craft is an odd one, because it doesn't require much downtime, but it does require you to get all those Craft points. Those are the real limiter (until you Charm your way past it, at which point it's the materials needed that are the limiter).</div> </div> </div> </div>You can minmax your character and get a couple hundred of those in a single day just by making arrows<br /> <br /> Also this is why the best crafting projects involve carving mountains into your chosen product","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T18:47:20-07:00","id":1209849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209771#post1209771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at that thread, the question wasn't &quot;can you decrease the interval at all?&quot; but rather &quot;can you decrease the interval in exchange for having 'negative Means' [i.e. reducing the terminus of the project]?&quot;\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026If you look at that thread, you can see that I was one of the people who posted in it. Right there, on the first page. I was <i>there.</i><br /> <br /> My point wasn't that the devs specifically set a blanket ban on interval-reducers altogether; it was a request for a cite of them being okay with interval-reducers, because the last time I remembered seeing someone ask for one, they specifically stepped in and said no.<br /> <br /> My understanding of workings is that they're intended to feel like pretty significant undertakings (one of the reasons they're called <i>work</i>ings!), and part of what makes it feel significant is the amount of time one must invest in it. Having to set aside at least a week generally keeps it from being something one does lightly. Being able to knock that down to days or hours or minutes would definitely take away from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-21-2018, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T19:25:23-07:00","id":1209864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209849#post1209849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of workings is that they're intended to feel like pretty significant undertakings (one of the reasons they're called <i>work</i>ings!), and part of what makes it feel significant is the amount of time one must invest in it. Having to set aside at least a week generally keeps it from being something one does lightly. Being able to knock that down to days or hours or minutes would definitely take away from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do understand that but at the same time, if a working is a piece of piss it should be a piece of piss, if you can triple the goal number in one check it shouldn't be forced to take a week, it's just silly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T19:48:31-07:00","id":1209870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209864#post1209864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do understand that but at the same time, if a working is a piece of piss it should be a piece of piss, if you can triple the goal number in one check it shouldn't be forced to take a week, it's just silly</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, though - no working is a piece of piss.<br /> <br /> \u2026excepting the Litterbox Elemental I whipped up. But that doesn't count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T20:15:42-07:00","id":1209875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209870#post1209870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing, though - no working is a piece of piss.<br /> <br /> \u2026excepting the Litterbox Elemental I whipped up. But that doesn't count.</div> </div> </div> </div>Au contraire, most of them are, they're just time consuming pieces of piss","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T02:02:47-07:00","id":1209950,"title":"","content":"I don't agree most of them are, but I guess since you're talking about &quot;tripling the goal in one roll&quot; you're talking about Terrestrial 1 workings? Which are pretty minor.<br /> <br /> I suppose I wouldn't find it problematic to do something like halve the time if you get double the successes. That seems reasonable.<br /> <br /> One thing we did find is that, because workings can be used to solve so many problems, it can be tempting to go &quot;hmm, I'll spend some Solar XP* and just solve this issue with a working.&quot;<br /> Which the non-Sorcerer players complained about.<br /> <br /> *If you're a Solar sorcerer, everything less than Celestial 3 is 1-2xp, so it's not like you even have to spend a significant amount of XP.<br /> <br /> But the time limits that. Sure, you can probably solve this problem with sorcery, but do you have time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T02:43:47-07:00","id":1209959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209950#post1209950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the time limits that. Sure, you can probably solve this problem with sorcery, but do you have time?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more of the opinion that the working system needs to be redesigned so there is actually a chance at failure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T03:07:18-07:00","id":1209962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209959#post1209959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more of the opinion that the working system needs to be redesigned so there is actually a chance at failure</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dice are <i>inclined</i> to give you about half your pool in successes, but a smart player doesn't <i>dare</i> get complacent about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T03:44:50-07:00","id":1209969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209962#post1209962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dice are <i>inclined</i> to give you about half your pool in successes, but a smart player doesn't <i>dare</i> get complacent about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, it's just so easy, with a week long duration a full excellency is pretty safe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23635-lion-hamster","name":"Lion Hamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T04:09:30-07:00","id":1209976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209959#post1209959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm more of the opinion that the working system needs to be redesigned so there is actually a chance at failure</div> </div> </div> </div>Welllllllll....<br /> I do see where you're coming from. I've never actually seen people fail workings (if they think failure is likely, they don't try, because it wastes so much time), though I did succeed with a botch once (so my shadow ran off to become a creepy monster).<br /> <br /> But doing a high-level working with Finesse 5 is very difficult. My friend's PC, who's just recently become a sorcerer, is trying to gain control of a curse upon her (which turns her into a fox every night), and she certainly could pass, but the issue is she wants to do it with Finesse 5 (to gain complete control of it), but it's a Celestial Working, and she's a Terrestrial sorcerer, and Finesse 7 is <i>way</i> too difficult for her. Even if she had a max-ed out dice pool (which she does not), that'd be an average of about 4 threshold successes per roll, which is not enough to manage before the Terminus. And with Finesse 1, there's the problem that the end-result is unreliable, and may cause other issues.<br /> <br /> Out of interest, in your games are sorcerers generally doing Terrestrial Workings?<br /> <br /> Because those are very easy (and not very significant), but most of the Workings PCs in games I play/run want to do are Celestial, which are a lot trickier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-22-2018, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T08:26:30-07:00","id":1210034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lion Hamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1209875#post1209875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Au contraire, most of them are, they're just time consuming pieces of piss</div> </div> </div> </div>That's you, again, being reductionist to the point of warping your perception away from the system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T11:38:38-07:00","id":1210102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1208763#post1208763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We got sample evocations and artifacts, but the expectation is that people will heavily homebrew and customize. Similarly, in Sorcery, we got few sample initiations and spells, but the expectation is also that people will heavily customize.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly my understanding of the system. I have had players who have looked at the Sorcery section and said, \u201cBut I don\u2019t want to shoot butterflies at people! That\u2019s lame!\u201d In a similar fashion, someone may want more out of their goremaul than the weird spirit eating thing in Arms of the Chosen.<br /> <br /> I think all of these things have been created to be ideas - hooks - that stir your own creativity. The designers could have made this more clear, however. They could have also presented a series of mechanical bookends for each power level to show what the basic considerations of balance should be. For example, Death of Obsidian Butterflies does (Essence + extra successes) damage on a decisive attack made with (Perception + Occult). The book could have explained when damaging spells should be used as withering attacks (a blast of wind, maybe), when they are better served by decisive attacks, and how much damage is appropriate for terrestrial, celestial, and solar levels of power.<br /> <br /> They have essentially done this with the examples that they have given, but the lack of encouragement to do exactly that in the book itself means that almost all characters that want to play with sorcery, and who think of that in anything close to D&amp;D terms, almost ALL pick up Death of Obsidian Butterflies as their primary attack spell, and I think that\u2019s regrettable. If anything, a spell like that should be the calling card of a VERY unique sorcerer, not the Exalted version of Magic Missile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T12:30:51-07:00","id":1210120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1203337-disconnect-between-sorcery-in-lore-and-the-encouraged-use-in-game?p=1210102#post1210102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u201cBut I don\u2019t want to shoot butterflies at people! That\u2019s lame!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThey understand that those butterflies are made from volcanic glass, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PneumaPilot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could have also presented a series of mechanical bookends for each power level to show what the basic considerations of balance should be. For example, Death of Obsidian Butterflies does (Essence + extra successes) damage on a decisive attack made with (Perception + Occult). The book could have explained when damaging spells should be used as withering attacks (a blast of wind, maybe), when they are better served by decisive attacks, and how much damage is appropriate for terrestrial, celestial, and solar levels of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't think there's really a simple formula for these things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T12:43:04-07:00","id":1210126,"title":"","content":"Also, I don't know about you but against individual combatants I'd take Flight of the Brilliant Raptor over Death of Obisidian Butterflies any day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts